[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Define the original-content provenance control that makes each later authored
[stderr] content package auditable before it enters a build. The control supplies a
[stderr] provenance-record format, source-asset manifest input, validator contract, and
[stderr] human creative-review disposition without creating art, audio, story, or legal
[stderr] approval.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0005 provides the versioned content package, asset/provenance-manifest schema,
[stderr] and validator boundary. It is the implementation dependency. Human creative
[stderr] review is mandatory for every authored package; legal or licensing review,
[stderr] where applicable, remains under GATE-0007 and cannot be inferred or automated.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `assets/source-manifest.*` provenance input format for later authored
[stderr]   content/assets.
[stderr] - `docs/original-content-review.md` review checklist and recorded disposition.
[stderr] - `tests/content/provenance.*` missing-field and review-state fixtures.
[stderr] - Provenance manifest, review disposition data, and provenance-validator input
[stderr]   contract.
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0005 retains content-schema and registry ownership. This task owns only the
[stderr] evidence required to admit later authored material; it does not own assets,
[stderr] licences, gameplay content, or release packaging.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Require a stable content-package reference and a complete provenance record
[stderr] for every later authored content, visual, audio, localisation, map, dialogue,
[stderr] or other expressive entry. The record must identify the entry, its authoring
[stderr] source/type, original-work assertion, any declared permitted source or licence
[stderr] reference when applicable, review status, reviewer identity/role placeholder,
[stderr] review date placeholder, and a human creative-review disposition. Keep the
[stderr] functional reference boundary explicit: a compact party-based turn-adventure
[stderr] scope may inform function only; names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts,
[stderr] UI flows, interaction choreography, and other expression must be original.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The validator rejects a missing record, missing required fields, unmatched
[stderr] content reference, invalid disposition, or an entry not marked ready after
[stderr] human creative review. It must not infer originality from an asset filename,
[stderr] automatically clear legal rights, or create substitute content. A reviewer may
[stderr] record a hold or reject disposition; only the human reviewer can record the
[stderr] creative-review outcome. Where a declared source signals licensing or legal
[stderr] review, retain GATE-0007 rather than allowing a technical validator to approve
[stderr] it.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] The provenance control is shared content metadata and has no separate web or
[stderr] PWA behaviour. Responsive web and installed PWA consume only content that has
[stderr] passed the same provenance validation; installation, caching, and packaging do
[stderr] not create a provenance exception.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Non-goals
[stderr] 
[stderr] Do not create or select art, audio, dialogue, maps, story, UI, fonts, icons,
[stderr] assets, licences, legal advice, automated legal clearance, release packaging,
[stderr] or target-specific content. Do not treat a reference, filename, or automated
[stderr] check as human creative or legal approval.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Asset assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. This is a control and review contract for
[stderr] future asset-required work; it creates no product asset. Do not create or
[stderr] reserve visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map,
[stderr] or other incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Verification
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Run validator fixtures proving missing provenance, required-field omissions,
[stderr]   unmatched IDs, invalid review dispositions, and unreviewed entries are
[stderr]   rejected before content admission.
[stderr] - Run a valid synthetic record fixture with an explicit original-work assertion
[stderr]   and recorded human creative-review disposition; it must be traceable to its
[stderr]   content-package reference.
[stderr] - Review the checklist against the originality boundary and prove that it
[stderr]   retains functional-only reference use and records a hold for any applicable
[stderr]   GATE-0007 legal/licensing concern.
[stderr] - Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its
[stderr]   metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the
[stderr]   manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0011 and never renumber or replace it.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Evidence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Retain rejected-fixture results, the valid synthetic record and reviewer
[stderr] disposition, the originality-boundary checklist result, any GATE-0007 hold,
[stderr] and the successful loader and manifest-comparison record.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Missing or invalid provenance records prevent later authored content from
[stderr]   entering a build; validated records remain traceable to their package entry.
[stderr] - A human creative review disposition is recorded for each authored package;
[stderr]   automated validation does not claim creative, legal, or licensing approval.
[stderr] - The original-expression boundary and any applicable GATE-0007 review remain
[stderr]   explicit, with no asset, audio, or copied expression introduced.
