[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Add deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for
[stderr] +the SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,
[stderr] +blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without
[stderr] +introducing concrete campaign content.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter
[stderr] +and reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns
[stderr] +fixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state
[stderr] +rules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.
[stderr] +- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.
[stderr] +- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Provide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,
[stderr] +reward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;
[stderr] +stale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a
[stderr] +stable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never
[stderr] +mutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid
[stderr] +abstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep
[stderr] +fixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +These are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,
[stderr] +responsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,
[stderr] +real player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete
[stderr] +content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require
[stderr] +no product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,
[stderr] +textures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect
[stderr] +trigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product
[stderr] +cues.
[stderr] +
