[stderr] +- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including
[stderr] +  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.
[stderr] +- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract
[stderr] +  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.
[stderr] +- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against
[stderr] +  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run
[stderr] +comparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected
[stderr] +  coverage and does not mutate state.
[stderr] +- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate
[stderr] +  grants are repeat-safe.
[stderr] +- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,
[stderr] +  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.
