[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,
[stderr] +asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a
[stderr] +developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly
[stderr] +and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This
[stderr] +handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion
[stderr] +resolves GATE-0004 or human review.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.
[stderr] +- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.
[stderr] +- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,
[stderr] +encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content
[stderr] +package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks
[stderr] +concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance
[stderr] +review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or
[stderr] +documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,
[stderr] +accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the
[stderr] +shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume
