[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Specify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon
[stderr] +route, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected
[stderr] +inventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration
[stderr] +rules, not authored story or presentation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015
[stderr] +owns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This
[stderr] +contract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.
[stderr] +GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.
[stderr] +- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,
[stderr] +  and the campaign-completion command.
[stderr] +- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Accept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final
[stderr] +state: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required
[stderr] +encounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate
[stderr] +expected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits
[stderr] +one stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request
[stderr] +returns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending
[stderr] +effects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed
[stderr] +rejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render
[stderr] +its state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,
[stderr] +and installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,
[stderr] +audio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.
[stderr] +Do not resolve GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration
[stderr] +contract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,
[stderr] +portraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or
[stderr] +mix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not
[stderr] +create incidental cues.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending
[stderr] +  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.
[stderr] +- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests
[stderr] +  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to
[stderr] +  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the
[stderr] +manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.
[stderr] +- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and
[stderr] +  reward grants cannot occur.
[stderr] +- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain
[stderr] +  outside this contract.
