[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the
[stderr] +town, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain
[stderr] +contracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;
[stderr] +do not create product expression during authoring.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the
[stderr] +provenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013–R0016
[stderr] +provide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This
[stderr] +contract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.
[stderr] +GATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of
[stderr] +concrete authored content; neither is resolved here.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and
[stderr] +  `tests/content/campaign*`.
[stderr] +- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest
[stderr] +  entries for the reserved asset groups.
[stderr] +- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Assemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the
[stderr] +campaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must
[stderr] +have a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as
[stderr] +defined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,
[stderr] +whose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is
[stderr] +recorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.
[stderr] +The package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define
[stderr] +new gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks
[stderr] +cannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.
[stderr] +Rendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior
[stderr] +remain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,
[stderr] +dialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.
[stderr] +Do not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve
[stderr] +GATE-0004 or the human review.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:
[stderr] +`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),
[stderr] +`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and
[stderr] +`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They
[stderr] +appear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of
[stderr] +truth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,
[stderr] +visual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under
[stderr] +`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before
[stderr] +admission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit
[stderr] +human creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated
[stderr] +by this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and
[stderr] +style version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character
[stderr] +  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.
[stderr] +- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a
