[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,
[stderr] +asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a
[stderr] +developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly
[stderr] +and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This
[stderr] +handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion
[stderr] +resolves GATE-0004 or human review.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.
[stderr] +- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.
[stderr] +- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,
[stderr] +encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content
[stderr] +package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks
[stderr] +concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance
[stderr] +review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or
[stderr] +documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,
[stderr] +accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the
[stderr] +shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume
[stderr] +the same campaign rules and validated content, but their UI, input adapters,
[stderr] +cache/install/update lifecycle, and release delivery are not SHARD-02 work.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not implement UI, PWA delivery, browser tests, rendering, input mappings,
[stderr] +asset production, audio, release claims, product changes, or gate approvals.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this documentation creates no visual or
[stderr] +source asset. Do not create or reserve any product asset; `asset_ids` remains
[stderr] +blank. R0018 remains the sole owner of its reserved campaign asset IDs.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no cue, playback behavior, or mix belongs
[stderr] +to this documentation handoff. Keep audio metadata blank/default and create no
[stderr] +audio asset.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Cross-check the ownership index against IMP-0013 through IMP-0020 and
[stderr] +  R0013–R0019, confirming every shared domain has one stated owner/boundary.
[stderr] +- Confirm GATE-0004, human provenance review, R0018 asset reservation, and the
[stderr] +  SHARD-03 UI/PWA boundary are explicit and unresolved where required.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, requirement IDs, dependencies, provenance, and ownership
[stderr] +  with IMP-0020 and the manifest without making release-readiness claims.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain the ownership cross-check, gate/provenance review record, SHARD-03
[stderr] +handoff review, and manifest/catalogue comparison.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- The documentation assigns SHARD-02 domain ownership and its interfaces
[stderr] +  without claiming UI or PWA implementation ownership.
[stderr] +- GATE-0004, the human provenance review, and R0018 asset-reservation boundary
[stderr] +  are explicit and unresolved.
[stderr] +- SHARD-03 receives a clear documented handoff for UI, input, accessibility,
[stderr] +  responsive web, and installed-PWA responsibilities.
