projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-128-### FEX-13 — Original minimal content package and authoring validation
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-129-
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-130-- **Target / ownership:** Shared content; `content/base`, `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}`, `assets/source-manifest.*`; no browser spec until rendered by FEX-02–FEX-05.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:131:- **Player-visible behaviour:** The complete first-release route is original Larkspur Reach → Glassroot Hollow → restored beacon ending, with authored dialogue, tutorial, quests, encounters, items, rewards, base locale, and provenance records.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-132-- **Invariants / validation:** Package version, IDs, references, localisation keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability validate before release. The opening-to-ending graph must be reachable; invalid/missing asset or reference fixtures fail without shipping. Provenance records identify original creation/source status.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-133-- **Scope boundary:** Exactly one town, one dungeon, short ending, and offline campaign. No imported branded material, expansion areas, live events, player-created content, or unapproved monetisation/analytics.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:134:- **Acceptance evidence:** Valid minimum package, invalid-reference fixtures, reachability test, authored provenance review, and manual original-design checklist.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-135-
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-136-### FEX-14 — Release safety and quality evidence
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-137-
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:138:- **Target / ownership:** Shared release/QA documentation and checks; `scripts/release-check.*`, `docs/{quality-plan,test-matrix,security-and-provenance,player-guide,accessibility,privacy-and-recovery,release-runbook,rollback,content-authoring}.md`; browser evidence `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-14-release-evidence.spec.*`.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-139-- **Player-visible behaviour:** Help explains controls, save/recovery, accessibility, privacy, version/cache status, and support paths. Release copy makes no promise beyond approved browser/device, performance, localisation, or assistive-technology decisions.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:140:- **Invariants / validation:** Build assets are hashed; CSP/static host headers, parser/size bounds, dependency/license/provenance review, and client-secret scan pass. Quality evidence maps every contract to deterministic, integration, browser, and required manual checks; fixtures never write player data.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-141-- **Recovery / rollback:** A known-good build can be restored through the documented rollback procedure without changing player saves. Unsupported/corrupt hostile content and save payloads fail safely.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-142-- **Acceptance evidence:** CI-equivalent command transcript, release/security reports, browser smoke start/save/resume evidence, completed manual matrix fields, and known-good rollback dry run.
projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-143-
--
