ojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-7-source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#5-inventory-party-progression-and-economy,specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md:8:source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0016\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-9-authoring_batch: B0007\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-10-factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-11-asset_impact: not_applicable\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-31-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-32-R0004 provides immutable state and idempotent commands; R0015 provides stable\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-33-reward resolution and one-time reward IDs. Their implementation ownership\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md:34:remains intact. GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for authored item and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-35-progression shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-36-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-37-## Ownership\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-63-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-64-Do not author items, party members, progression values, inventory UI, crafting,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-65-trading, purchases, destructive discard, art, audio, maps, remote state, or\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md:66:browser/PWA behavior. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-67-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-68-## Asset assessment\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-69-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-84-  and that missing/ineligible/stale commands preserve the exact prior state.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-85-- Prove duplicate reward IDs do not apply twice and protected required items\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-86-  cannot be lost in a way that removes the required abstract route.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md:87:- Compare metadata, requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance with\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md:88:  IMP-0016 and R0016's manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-89-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-90-## Evidence\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-91-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-92-Retain inventory/progression rejection fixtures, duplicate-reward and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-93-protected-item invariant results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and the\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md:94:unresolved GATE-0004 record.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-95-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-96-## Acceptance criteria\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md-97-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md-112-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md-113-## Content and interaction review checklist\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md-114-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md:115:Before a content or UI change ships, review it against this contract: original provenance; clear next action and empty/error copy; keyboard, touch, mouse, gamepad, and semantic assistive-input operation; visible focus and accurate accessible names; contrast and non-colour cues; 44 CSS-px touch targets; 200% text/reflow; captions and reduced motion; safe save/update/recovery behaviour; destructive confirmation; and consent/minimisation for any privacy-sensitive interface.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md-116-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md-117-## Open decisions retained for approval\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md-118-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-128-### FEX-13 \u2014 Original minimal content package and authoring validation\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-129-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-130-- **Target / ownership:** Shared content; `content/base`, `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}`, `assets/source-manifest.*`; no browser spec until rendered by FEX-02\u2013FEX-05.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:131:- **Player-visible behaviour:** The complete first-release route is original Larkspur Reach \u2192 Glassroot Hollow \u2192 restored beacon ending, with authored dialogue, tutorial, quests, encounters, items, rewards, base locale, and provenance records.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-132-- **Invariants / validation:** Package version, IDs, references, localisation keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability validate before release. The opening-to-ending graph must be reachable; invalid/missing asset or reference fixtures fail without shipping. Provenance records identify original creation/source status.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-133-- **Scope boundary:** Exactly one town, one dungeon, short ending, and offline campaign. No imported branded material, expansion areas, live events, player-created content, or unapproved monetisation/analytics.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:134:- **Acceptance evidence:** Valid minimum package, invalid-reference fixtures, reachability test, authored provenance review, and manual original-design checklist.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-135-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-136-### FEX-14 \u2014 Release safety and quality evidence\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-137-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:138:- **Target / ownership:** Shared release/QA documentation and checks; `scripts/release-check.*`, `docs/{quality-plan,test-matrix,security-and-provenance,player-guide,accessibility,privacy-and-recovery,release-runbook,rollback,content-authoring}.md`; browser evidence `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-14-release-evidence.spec.*`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-139-- **Player-visible behaviour:** Help explains controls, save/recovery, accessibility, privacy, version/cache status, and support paths. Release copy makes no promise beyond approved browser/device, performance, localisation, or assistive-technology decisions.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md:140:- **Invariants / validation:** Build assets are hashed; CSP/static host headers, parser/size bounds, dependency/license/provenance review, and client-secret scan pass. Quality evidence maps every contract to deterministic, integration, browser, and required manual checks; fixtures never write player data.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-141-- **Recovery / rollback:** A known-good build can be restored through the documented rollback procedure without changing player saves. Unsupported/corrupt hostile content and save payloads fail safely.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-142-- **Acceptance evidence:** CI-equivalent command transcript, release/security reports, browser smoke start/save/resume evidence, completed manual matrix fields, and known-good rollback dry run.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/07-feature-experience-contracts.md-143-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-5-dependencies: R0005,R0006\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-6-requirement_ids: REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-7-source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md:8:source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0007\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-9-authoring_batch: B0005\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-10-factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-11-asset_impact: not_applicable\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-31-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-32-## Dependencies\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-33-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md:34:R0005 owns the versioned content and provenance schema boundary. R0006 owns\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-35-the local save, validation, current-pointer, known-good retention, and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-36-quarantine protocol. Both are implementation dependencies. Retain GATE-0003 /\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-37-DEC-0003: a human decision is required for the supported migration window,\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-97-- Prove the runner has no storage, network, clock, cache, pointer-promotion,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-98-  or mutation dependency; web and PWA adapter fixtures use the same API.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-99-- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md:100:  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-101-  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0007 and never renumber or replace it.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-102-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md-103-## Evidence\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-1-# Requirements traceability matrix\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-2-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:3:`IMP-*` and implementation-runbook IDs are intentionally **unassigned**: F012 owns that allocation. \u201cPlanned evidence\u201d names the eventual independently reviewable evidence; it is not current implementation proof.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-4-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-5-| Requirements | Journeys | Components / contracts | Planned implementation IDs | Final evidence |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-6-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md:7:| REQ-0001\u20130002, REQ-0008 | J1\u2013J3 | content/campaign/scene; FDN-05, FEX-02,03,13 | DM-03,04,08,11,14; IMP unassigned | content validation, reachability, provenance review, playthrough |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-8-| REQ-0003 | J2 | combat/rewards; FDN-05, FEX-04 | DM-09,14; IMP unassigned | deterministic combat and browser journey |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-9-| REQ-0004 | J4 | inventory/party/rewards; FEX-05 | DM-10,14; IMP unassigned | inventory fixtures and UI journey |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-10-| REQ-0005 | J1\u2013J2 | tutorial/shell; FEX-01,04 | DM-08,13,14; IMP unassigned | tutorial first-battle/save evidence |\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/traceability-matrix.md-14-| REQ-0011, NFR-0001, NFR-0011 | J7 | PWA/cache/release; FEX-12,14, QOR-04\u201305,08 | DM-17\u201320; IMP unassigned | off