ition, source/exported variants, and an owning R contract. Essential meaning must have a text, accessible-name, or non-colour equivalent. Asset tasks own content/provenance; PWA delivery owns hashing and caching. A family is complete only when original provenance, variants, responsive readability, and accessibility are verified.\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-58-story/lore, dialogue, maps, music, layouts, menus, combat screens, interaction\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-59-choreography, or distinctive presentation. All planned content and assets must\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-60-be independently original, warm hand-painted fantasy with readable silhouettes\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md:61:and a restrained palette, supported by provenance records and later human\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-62-review.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-63-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-64-## Execution order and dependencies\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-66-| Stage | Required outcome | Inputs / dependency | Cannot proceed without |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-67-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-68-| F011 | Canonical `REQ-*`, `NFR-*`, `DEC-*`, `RISK-*`, `GATE-*` system and traceability | This handoff and all specifications/planning 05\u201309 | Recording, not deciding, open choices |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md:69:| F012 | Bounded `IMP-*` catalogue, ownership, and acyclic graph | Completed F011 | Requirement traceability and named domain shards |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/10-authoring-handoff.md-70-| F013 | Persistent B/R allocation ledger and context packets | Completed F