ts.md-202-  support approval is not implied by a documentation check and requires its\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-203-  authorised reviewer record.\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-237-| Gate | Required evidence | Hold when |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-238-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-239-| Candidate identity and compatibility | Version/build hash; content/save schema versions and supported ranges; known-good rollback target | Identity, hash, compatibility, or rollback target is missing or incompatible. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md:240:| Trust and privacy | QOR-01 artifact secret scan/configuration result; QOR-02 consent/redaction/input-safety results; provenance/dependency review | A secret finding, unsafe parser/rendering result, missing consent/redaction evidence, or unresolved provenance/dependency risk exists. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-241-| Health and recovery | QOR-03 recovery evidence; QOR-04 save/migration/quarantine/cache-retention tests and rollback dry run | A fault lacks a safe path, save/recovery test fails, or rollback/recovery evidence is absent. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-242-| Quality and accessibility | QOR-07 CI/browser/manual evidence, with approved target matrix and all required contract mappings | A required check is fail, blocked, not run, stale, or lacks reviewable evidence. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/08-quality-operations-contracts.md-243-| Performance and environment | QOR-05 validated configuration, hash/size report, and approved-matrix measurement against approved budget | Required environment/budget/matrix evidence is unapproved, absent, or over budget without authorised disposition. |\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-4-  \"source_of_truth\": \"../INITIAL.md\",\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-5-  \"reference_boundary\": \"Final Fantasy V is scope-only; no protected expression may be copied.\",\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-6-  \"requirements\": [\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json:7:    {\"id\":\"REQ-0001\",\"title\":\"Original 2D single-player fantasy RPG\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Brief: creation/category\",\"rationale\":\"Defines P0 product\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"playthrough + provenance review\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-8-    {\"id\":\"REQ-0002\",\"title\":\"One-town, one-dungeon campaign with ending\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Brief: creation/capabilities\",\"rationale\":\"Fixed release content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"content reachability/playthrough\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-9-    {\"id\":\"REQ-0003\",\"title\":\"Party turn combat and defeat recovery\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Brief; J2\",\"rationale\":\"Core loop\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"combat tests/J2\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-10-    {\"id\":\"REQ-0004\",\"title\":\"Safe inventory/progression\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Brief; J4\",\"rationale\":\"Required capability\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"inventory tests/J4\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-26-    {\"id\":\"NFR-0005\",\"title\":\"Separate settings persistence\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"J6\",\"rationale\":\"Safe preferences\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"failure test\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-27-    {\"id\":\"NFR-0006\",\"title\":\"Minimal consent-gated diagnostics\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Brief/QOR-02\",\"rationale\":\"Privacy\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"verification\":\"redaction test\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-28-    {\"id\":\"NFR-0007\",\"title\":\"Content validation\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Feature/technical contracts\",\"rationale\":\"Completable content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"validator\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json:29:    {\"id\":\"NFR-0008\",\"title\":\"Original-design provenance\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Brief boundary\",\"rationale\":\"No copied expression\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"verification\":\"provenance review\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-30-    {\"id\":\"NFR-0009\",\"title\":\"Approved performance measurement\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"source\":\"Web/QOR-05\",\"rationale\":\"No unsupported claims\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"verification\":\"approved matrix\",\"status\":\"proposed\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-31-    {\"id\":\"NFR-0010\",\"title\":\"Shared core with isolated adaptations\",\"priority\":\"P0\",\"source\":\"Cross-platform decision\",\"rationale\":\"Parity\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"verification\":\"architecture review\",\"status\":\"accepted\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/requirements.json-32-    {\"id\":\"NFR-0011\",\"title\":\"Release compatibility and rollback\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"source\":\"PWA/release\",\"rationale\":\"Safe delivery\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"verification\":\"release evidence\",\"status\":\"proposed\"},\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md-5-dependencies:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md-6-requirement_ids: NFR-0010,NFR-0012\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md-7-source_specifications: specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition,specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md:8:source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md-9-authoring_batch: B0001\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md-10-factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md-11-asset_impact: not_applicable\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-1-# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-2-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:3:This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-4-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-5-## Dispatcher checkpoint \u2014 D0002\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-6-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:7:D0002 expanded the now-authorable `SHARD-02` exactly once into eight contracts\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:8:(`IMP-0013`\u2013`IMP-0020`), below its 250-record limit. `GATE-0004` remains on\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-9-each affected contract as an implementation gate and was not treated as an\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-10-authoring blocker. The eight contracts are allocated once between B0007 and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:11:B0008 (four outputs each), with asset reservation only in R0018. SHARD-03 and\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-12-SHARD-04 remain queued, so [`D0003`](../authoring-runbooks/D0003.md) is the\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-13-sole successor. Counters now append at B0009/R0021; accepted work is unchanged.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-14-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-15-## Dispatcher checkpoint \u2014 D0001\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-16-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:17:D0001 expanded no chapter and allocated no B/R contracts. `SHARD-02` is the\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:18:first queued chapter, but `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` remains unresolved; `SHARD-03`\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-19-and `SHARD-04` retain their predecessor and gate blocks, while `SHARD-05` stays\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-20-held pending explicit authorisation. Every current catalogue contract\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:21:(`IMP-0001` through `IMP-0012`) is allocated exactly once. The dispatcher\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-22-therefore created [`D0002`](../authoring-runbooks/D0002.md) as the sole\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-23-successor, without advancing B/R counters or modifying accepted work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-24-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-30-| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-31-| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-32-| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:33:| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-34-| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:35:| 7 | B0007 | R0013, R0014, R0015, R0016 | After B0003; GATE-0004 retained | Validate domain-state seams and non-asset boundaries |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:36:| 8 | B0008 | R0017, R0018, R0019, R0020 | After B0007; GATE-0004/provenance retained | Validate campaign integration, asset reservation, and SHARD-03 handoff |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-37-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:38:The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-39-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-40-## Contract allocation and asset assessment\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-41-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-42-| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-43-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:44:| R0001 | IMP-0001 | B0001 | `runbooks/R0001.md` | not applicable \u2014 tooling boundary only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:45:| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:46:| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:47:| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:48:| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:49:| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:50:| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:51:| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:52:| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:53:| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:54:| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:55:| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:56:| R0013\u2013R0017, R0019\u2013R0020 | IMP-0013\u2013IMP-0017, IMP-0019\u2013IMP-0020 | B0007/B0008 | `runbooks/R0013.md`\u2013`R0020.md` | not applicable \u2014 contract, fixture, integration, and documentation work only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:57:| R0018 | IMP-0018 | B0008 | `runbooks/R0018.md` | required \u2014 reserves original campaign asset groups; authoring must not create them |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-58-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-59-No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-60-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-61-## Author packet and resume rules\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-62-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:63:Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-64-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:65:At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-66-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-67-## Queued expansion chapters\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-68-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-69-| Chapter | Future allocation point | State |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-70-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:71:| SHARD-02 \u2014 Campaign content and domain logic | Wave 2 authoring allocation; GATE-0004 retained for implementation | expanded |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:72:| SHARD-03 \u2014 Session, UI, input, and accessibility | Wave 3 after SHARD-02 and GATE-0002/0003/0004 | queued |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:73:| SHARD-04 \u2014 PWA delivery, performance, operations, release evidence | Wave 4 after SHARD-02/03 and GATE-0002/0005/0007 | queued |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-74-| SHARD-05 \u2014 Connected-scope decision package | Only explicit authorisation after GATE-0006; no P0 R allocation | hold |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-75-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manife