ed seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-54-| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-55-| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:56:| R0013\u2013R0017, R0019\u2013R0020 | IMP-0013\u2013IMP-0017, IMP-0019\u2013IMP-0020 | B0007/B0008 | `runbooks/R0013.md`\u2013`R0020.md` | not applicable \u2014 contract, fixture, integration, and documentation work only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:57:| R0018 | IMP-0018 | B0008 | `runbooks/R0018.md` | required \u2014 reserves original campaign asset groups; authoring must not create them |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-58-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-59-No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-4-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-5-```zsh\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md:6:python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-7-```\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-8-\n--\nsupervisor/tests/test_cli_resume.py-6-\nsupervisor/tests/test_cli_resume.py-7-from supervisor import cli\nsupervisor/tests/test_cli_resume.py:8:from supervisor.cli import START_STAGES, _authoring_output_errors, _can_recover_qwen, _collection_runbooks, _completion_banner, _expand_task_range, _initial_document, _project_database_for_runbook, _project_workspace, _qwen_session_to_resume, _recovered_qwen_event, _reopen_invalid_authoring_tasks, _resume_stage, _retry_stage, _run_collection_until_complete, _run_registered_collections, _run_summary, _should_skip_accepted_task, _unmet_dependencies\nsupervisor/tests/test_cli_resume.py-9-from supervisor.failure_summary import _deterministic_summary, summarize_failure\nsupervisor/tests/test_cli_resume.py-10-from supervisor.models import NextStep, RunEvent, Status, Task, TaskRun, WorkerResult\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md && sed -n '1,240p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py && rg -n -C 2 '\"'^## (2|3|4|5)'\"\\\\.|\"'^## Domain vocabulary|''^## Capability parity'\"' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md && sed -n '1,240p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n---\ntask_id: R0011\nsequence: 11\ntitle: Create original-content provenance control\ndependencies: R0005\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0008,NFR-0008\nsource_specifications: specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary,specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0011\nauthoring_batch: B0005\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the original-content provenance control that makes each later authored\ncontent package auditable before it enters a build. The control supplies a\nprovenance-record format, source-asset manifest input, validator contract, and\nhuman creative-review disposition without creating art, audio, story, or legal\napproval.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0005 provides the versioned content package, asset/provenance-manifest schema,\nand validator boundary. It is the implementation dependency. Human creative\nreview is mandatory for every authored package; legal or licensing review,\nwhere applicable, remains under GATE-0007 and cannot be inferred or automated.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `assets/source-manifest.*` provenance input format for later authored\n  content/assets.\n- `docs/original-content-review.md` review checklist and recorded disposition.\n- `tests/content/provenance.*` missing-field and review-state fixtures.\n- Provenance manifest, review disposition data, and provenance-validator input\n  contract.\n\nR0005 retains content-schema and registry ownership. This task owns only the\nevidence required to admit later authored material; it does not own assets,\nlicences, gameplay content, or release packaging.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nRequire a stable content-package reference and a complete provenance record\nfor every later authored content, visual, audio, localisation, map, dialogue,\nor other expressive entry. The record must identify the entry, its authoring\nsource/type, original-work assertion, any declared permitted source or licence\nreference when applicable, review status, reviewer identity/role placeholder,\nreview date placeholder, and a human creative-review disposition. Keep the\nfunctional reference boundary explicit: a compact party-based turn-adventure\nscope may inform function only; names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts,\nUI flows, interaction choreography, and other expression must be original.\n\nThe validator rejects a missing record, missing required fields, unmatched\ncontent reference, invalid disposition, or an entry not marked ready after\nhuman creative review. It must not infer originality from an asset filename,\nautomatically clear legal rights, or create substitute content. A reviewer may\nrecord a hold or reject disposition; only the human reviewer can record the\ncreative-review outcome. Where a declared source signals licensing or legal\nreview, retain GATE-0007 rather than allowing a technical validator to approve\nit.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nThe provenance control is shared content metadata and has no separate web or\nPWA behaviour. Responsive web and installed PWA consume only content that has\npassed the same provenance validation; installation, caching, and packaging do\nnot create a provenance exception.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not create or select art, audio, dialogue, maps, story, UI, fonts, icons,\nassets, licences, legal advice, automated legal clearance, release packaging,\nor target-specific content. Do not treat a reference, filename, or automated\ncheck as human creative or legal approval.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. This is a control and review contract for\nfuture asset-required work; it creates no product asset. Do not create or\nreserve visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map,\nor other incidental asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run validator fixtures proving missing provenance, required-field omissions,\n  unmatched IDs, invalid review dispositions, and unreviewed entries are\n  rejected before content admission.\n- Run a valid synthetic record fixture with an explicit original-work assertion\n  and recorded human creative-review disposition; it must be traceable to its\n  content-package reference.\n- Review the checklist against the originality boundary and prove that it\n  retains functional-only reference use and records a hold for any applicable\n  GATE-0007 legal/licensing concern.\n- Before recording the B0005 checkpoint, load this runbook and compare its\n  metadata, provenance, dependencies, requirement IDs, and ownership to the\n  manifest. Stop on a mismatch; retain R0011 and never renumber or replace it.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain rejected-fixture results, the valid synthetic record and reviewer\ndisposition, the originality-boundary checklist result, any GATE-0007 hold,\nand the successful loader and manifest-comparison record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Missing or invalid provenance records prevent later authored content from\n  entering a build; validated records remain traceable to their package entry.\n- A human creative review disposition is recorded for each authored package;\n  automated validation does not claim creative, legal, or licensing approval.\n- The original-expression boundary and any applicable GATE-0007 review remain\n  explicit, with no asset, audio, or copied expression introduced.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Structural quality gate for generated B-series and R-series runbooks.\n\nThis validates planning artefacts only; it is never product or release evidence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nREPOSITORY = ROOT.parents[1]\nMANIFEST_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"\nCATALOGUE_PATH = ROOT / \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"\nR_ID, F_ID = re.compile(r\"^R\\d{4}$\"), re.compile(r\"^F\\d{3}$\")\nLIST_FIELDS = {\n    \"dependencies\", \"requirement_ids\", \"source_specifications\",\n    \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_ids\", \"audio_ids\",\n    \"playwright_spec\", \"playwright_specs\",\n}\n\ndef values(value):\n    return value if isinstance(value, list) else ([value] if value else [])\n\ndef parse_value(value):\n    value = value.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\")\n    if value == \"[]\": return []\n    if value.startswith(\"[\") and value.endswith(\"]\"):\n        return [item.strip().strip(\"\\\"'\") for item in value[1:-1].split(\",\") if item.strip()]\n    return value\n\ndef front_matter(path):\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if not text.startswith(\"---\\n\"): return {}\n    end = text.find(\"\\n---\", 4)\n    if end < 0: return {}\n    result, key = {}, None\n    for line in text[4:end].splitlines():\n        if line.lstrip().startswith(\"-\") and key:\n            result.setdefault(key, []).append(parse_value(line.split(\"-\", 1)[1]))\n        elif \":\" in line:\n            key, value = line.split(\":\", 1); key = key.strip(); value = parse_value(value)\n            # Authoring runbooks use compact comma-delimited metadata for\n            # these schema-defined lists. Preserve scalar prose fields such as\n            # asset_brief verbatim while normalising only list metadata.\n            result[key] = [item.strip() for item in value.split(\",\") if item.strip()] if key in LIST_FIELDS and isinstance(value, str) else value\n    return result\n\ndef headings(path):\n    return {re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", match.group(1).lower()).strip(\"-\")\n            for match in re.finditer(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+?)\\s*$\", path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"), re.M)}\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--wave\", help=\"validate allocations through this B batch\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    manifest = json.loads(MANIFEST_PATH.read_text())\n    catalogue = json.loads(CATALOGUE_PATH.read_text())\n    batches = {b[\"id\"]: b for b in manifest[\"batches\"]}\n    contracts = manifest[\"r_contracts\"]\n    if args.wave:\n        if args.wave not in batches: parser.error(\"unknown B batch: \" + args.wave)\n        contracts = [c for c in contracts if batches.get(c.get(\"authoring_batch\"), {}).get(\"order\", 999) <= batches[args.wave][\"order\"]]\n    records = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in catalogue[\"contracts\"]}\n    errors, missing, blocked, unverified = [], [], [], []\n    def fail(text): errors.append(text)\n    ids = [c.get(\"id\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    if ids != sorted(ids): fail(\"manifest R IDs are not sequence ordered\")\n    for item, count in Counter(ids).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate manifest R ID \" + item)\n    paths = [c.get(\"output_path\", \"\") for c in contracts]\n    for item, count in Counter(paths).items():\n        if count > 1: fail(\"duplicate output path \" + item)\n    assets, browser_paths = {}, defaultdict(list)\n    # The authoring collection is part of the gate: each allocated batch must\n    # exist, identify itself, and be the sole owner of its manifest R IDs.\n    for batch_id, batch_record in batches.items():\n        batch_path = ROOT / \"authoring-runbooks\" / f\"{batch_id}.md\"\n        meta = front_matter(batch_path) if batch_path.is_file() else {}\n        if not meta: fail(f\"{batch_id}: missing or invalid B-series front matter\")\n        elif meta.get(\"task_id\") != batch_id: fail(f\"{batch_id}: task ID mismatch in authoring runbook\")\n        if len(batch_record.get(\"r_contract_ids\", [])) > 7: fail(f\"{batch_id}: exceeds seven-contract batch limit\")\n    for contract in contracts:\n        rid, batch = contract.get(\"id\", \"\"), contract.get(\"authoring_batch\", \"\")\n        if not R_ID.fullmatch(rid): fail(f\"invalid R ID {rid!r}\")\n        if batch not in batches or rid not in batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"r_contract_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: authoring batch ownership mismatch\")\n        catalogue_ids = values(contract.get(\"source_catalogue_ids\"))\n        if not catalogue_ids or contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") not in catalogue_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: missing or inconsistent catalogue provenance\")\n        for cid in catalogue_ids:\n            if cid not in records: fail(f\"{rid}: unknown catalogue ID {cid}\")\n        if contract.get(\"catalogue_id\") in records and not records[contract[\"catalogue_id\"]].get(\"requirement_ids\"): fail(f\"{rid}: catalogue record lacks requirement links\")\n        specs = values(contract.get(\"source_specifications\"))\n        if not specs: fail(f\"{rid}: missing source_specifications\")\n        for link in specs:\n            file_name, _, anchor = link.partition(\"#\"); source = ROOT / file_name\n            if not link.startswith(\"specification/\") or not source.is_file() or (anchor and anchor not in headings(source)):\n                fail(f\"{rid}: unresolved canonical specification link {link}\")\n        stages = values(contract.get(\"factory_stages\"))\n        if not stages or any(not F_ID.fullmatch(s) for s in stages): fail(f\"{rid}: invalid factory_stages\")\n        for dependency in values(contract.get(\"dependencies\")):\n            if dependency not in ids: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} is outside allocation\")\n            elif dependency >= rid: fail(f\"{rid}: dependency {dependency} does not precede contract\")\n        impact, asset_ids = contract.get(\"asset_impact\"), values(contract.get(\"asset_ids\"))\n        if impact not in {\"required\", \"not_applicable\"}: fail(f\"{rid}: invalid asset_impact\")\n        if \"asset_ids\" not in contract: fail(f\"{rid}: asset_ids absent\")\n        if impact == \"required\":\n            if not asset_ids or not contract.get(\"asset_brief\") or not contract.get(\"visual_style_version\"): fail(f\"{rid}: required assets lack IDs, brief, or style version\")\n            for asset in asset_ids:\n                if not re.fullmatch(r\"ASSET-[A-Z0-9-]+\", asset): fail(f\"{rid}: unstable asset ID {asset}\")\n                if asset in assets: fail(f\"asset {asset} ambiguously owned by {assets[asset]} and {rid}\")\n                assets[asset] = rid\n        elif asset_ids: fail(f\"{rid}: non-asset contract reserves asset IDs\")\n        if batches.get(batch, {}).get(\"state\") in {\"blocked_on_gate\", \"blocked\", \"repairable\"}: blocked.append(rid)\n        r_path = REPOSITORY / contract.get(\"output_path\", \"\")\n        if not r_path.is_file(): missing.append(rid); continue\n        meta = front_matter(r_path)\n        for field in (\"task_id\", \"sequence\", \"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if field not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks {field}\")\n        if \"requirement_ids\" not in meta: fail(f\"{rid}: {r_path.name} lacks requirement_ids\")\n        if meta.get(\"task_id\") != rid: fail(f\"{rid}: task ID mismatch\")\n        if values(meta.get(\"requirement_ids\")) != records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"requirement_ids\", []): fail(f\"{rid}: requirement_ids differ from catalogue\")\n        for field in (\"source_specifications\", \"source_catalogue_ids\", \"authoring_batch\", \"factory_stages\", \"asset_impact\", \"asset_ids\"):\n            if values(meta.get(field)) != values(contract.get(field)): fail(f\"{rid}: {field} differs from manifest\")\n        browser, specs = meta.get(\"browser_impact\", \"not_applicable\"), values(meta.get(\"playwright_spec\", meta.get(\"playwright_specs\")))\n        if browser == \"not_applicable\" and specs: fail(f\"{rid}: browser path on non-browser contract\")\n        if browser != \"not_applicable\" and (not specs or not set(records.get(contract.get(\"catalogue_id\"), {}).get(\"targets\", [])) & {\"web\", \"pwa\"}): fail(f\"{rid}: browser metadata outside browser behaviour scope\")\n        for spec in specs: browser_paths[spec].append(rid)\n        body = r_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if \"## Verification\" not in body: unverified.append(rid)\n        if not re.search(r\"^## Asset assessment\\s*$\", body, re.M | re.I): fail(f\"{rid}: missing explicit Asset assessment section\")\n    for path, owners in browser_paths.items():\n        if len(owners) > 1: fail(f\"duplicate browser test path {path}: {', '.join(owners)}\")\n    graph = {c[\"id\"]: values(c.get(\"dependencies\")) for c in contracts}; active, done = set(), set()\n    def visit(node):\n        if node in active: fail(\"unsupported circular dependency through \" + node); return\n        if node not in done:\n            active.add(node)\n            for dep in graph[node]:\n                if dep in graph: visit(dep)\n            active.remove(node); done.add(node)\n    for node in graph: visit(node)\n    # Discovered families need a canonical source and a category-appropriate\n    # catalogue/verification route. Explicitly held connected scope is a valid\n    # reviewed outcome, not a missing P0 implementation contract.\n    review = ROOT / \"specification/domain-completeness-review.md\"\n    for line in review.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith(\"|\") or line.startswith(\"| System\") or line.startswith(\"| ---\"): continue\n        cells = [cell.strip() for cell in line.split(\"|\")[1:-1]]\n        if len(cells) != 5: continue\n        family, source, _deps, authoring, decision = cells\n        if \"SPEC-\" not in source: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no specification chapter\")\n        if \"hold\" in decision.lower(): continue\n        keywords = [word.lower() for word in re.findall(r\"[A-Za-z]{5,}\", family)]\n        searchable = json.dumps(catalogue).lower()\n        if not any(word in searchable for word in keywords): fail(f\"domain family {family}: no catalogue traceability\")\n        if authoring.lower() not in {\"none\", \"n/a\"} and not authoring: fail(f\"domain family {family}: no content/authoring approach\")\n    allocated = {c.get(\"catalogue_id\") for c in contracts}\n    unallocated = [cid for cid in records if cid not in allocated]\n    print(\"Runbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\")\n    chapter_count = len(list((ROOT / \"specification\").glob(\"*.md\")))\n    source_link_count = sum(len(values(c.get(\"source_specifications\"))) for c in contracts)\n    print(f\"canonical specification chapters: {chapter_count}\")\n    print(f\"specification provenance links: {source_link_count}\")\n    for label, result in ((\"catalogue contracts\", list(records)), (\"manifest contracts\", ids), (\"R files missing\", missing), (\"blocked contracts\", blocked), (\"unverified contracts\", unverified), (\"unallocated catalogue contracts\", unallocated), (\"reserved asset IDs\", list(assets)), (\"browser test paths\", list(browser_paths))):\n        print(f\"{label}: {len(result)}\" + (\" (\" + \", \".join(sorted(result)) + \")\" if result else \"\"))\n    for error in errors: print(\"ERROR:\", error)\n    return 1 if errors or missing or unverified else 0\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())\n34-| J7 | Install, update, and recover from a fault: player retains a coherent playable version. | Install when browser allows \u2192 cache approved release \u2192 play offline \u2192 accept update at launch/menu after save boundary. | Installation prompt may be unavailable/declined without blocking web play; offline uncached assets state the requirement; cache refresh failure retains known-good cache; crash/error boundary offers retry, return to title, and safe recovery. Diagnostics are minimal and consent-gated where required; a player can decline or delete local diagnostic data without losing play. |\n35-\n36:## Domain vocabulary and state ownership\n37-\n38-| Term | Meaning / owner |\n--\n207-SLO until approved.\n208-\n209:## Capability parity and intentional differences\n210-\n211-| Capability | Responsive web | Installed PWA | Shared rule |\n# 02 \u2014 Feature model and release slices\n\n**Inputs:** [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md) and the canonical\n[project brief](../PROJECT_BRIEF.md). This document turns only the accepted\noffline-game scope into a model. It records connected and commercial requests\nas approval gates; it does not silently turn them into a first-release\ndependency.\n\n## Product outcome and personas\n\nThe first release is successful when a casual or adult player can start the\noriginal 2D fantasy adventure, complete an understandable first battle, save,\nreturn later without losing confirmed progress, finish the single town and\ndungeon story, and reach its short ending offline after installation or a\nsuccessful first asset download.\n\n| Persona | Job to be done | Success signal | Relevant journeys |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Casual story player | When I have a short session, help me understand what to do and make visible story progress without complex controls. | Starts, wins the tutorial battle, saves, and resumes a quest. | J1\u2013J4 |\n| Adult returning player | When I resume after interruption or a long gap, help me recover safely and understand my current objective. | Restored checkpoint is clear; no confirmed progress is silently lost. | J3, J5 |\n| Player with access needs | When I play on my chosen device, let me read, hear, see, and control the game in a comfortable way. | Can change supported text, caption, visual, and control options before or during play. | J1, J6 |\n| Offline PWA player | When connectivity changes or an update is available, let me keep playing the installed game without corrupting saves. | Cached release runs offline; update waits for a safe boundary. | J1, J5, J7 |\n\n## Core journeys\n\n| ID | Journey and outcome | Normal path | Empty / invalid / denied / offline / conflict / recovery / deletion handling |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| J1 | Start, orient, and configure: player reaches the town and knows the tutorial goal. | Open web game or installed PWA \u2192 choose new game \u2192 optional settings \u2192 readable dialogue and input hints \u2192 town. | No prior save shows New Game; unavailable gamepad falls back to listed keyboard/mouse/touch controls; unsupported input shows a non-blocking message. Offline launch is allowed only when the current assets are cached; otherwise explain that an initial download is needed. Declining optional diagnostics does not block play. |\n| J2 | Learn and win first combat: player understands the turn loop. | Accept first encounter \u2192 choose a legal party action \u2192 resolve enemy turn \u2192 win \u2192 receive reward and quest update. | Empty inventory/action lists show explanation; invalid/stale target or unavailable item is rejected without consuming a turn; defeated party reloads the latest safe checkpoint and explains the consequence. No network permission is needed. |\n| J3 | Explore and advance the campaign: player finishes town, dungeon, and ending. | Talk to characters \u2192 accept quest \u2192 traverse town/dungeon \u2192 resolve required encounter and objective \u2192 claim reward \u2192 see ending. | Locked exits state the missing quest condition; exhausted dialogue has a safe closing line; missing authored reference fails content validation and shows recoverable error rather than breaking state; optional reward absence never blocks completion. |\n| J4 | Manage items and progression: player can use earned resources correctly. | Open inventory \u2192 inspect item \u2192 use/equip only where legal \u2192 see immediate feedback \u2192 close back to play. | Empty inventory has an explicit empty state; invalid use, full/limited capacity (if authored), or ineligible target preserves inventory; quest items cannot be discarded if that would make a required path impossible. Deletion/discard is not a first-release capability unless an authored safe rule is later approved. |\n| J5 | Save, load, and recover: player can leave and return safely. | Manual save or checkpoint completes atomically \u2192 resume chooses latest valid save \u2192 state restores at a safe scene boundary. | No save slot shows explanation; corrupt/incompatible candidate is quarantined, never overwritten, and falls back to the last valid checkpoint or new game; storage denial/quota exposes retry and export/support guidance where feasible; interrupted write keeps prior confirmed save. Local cache and any future remote copy conflict resolve only with explicit player choice; remote sync is not first release. Deleting a save requires confirmation and removes only that selected local save. |\n| J6 | Adjust accessibility and feedback: player can make the game usable. | Open settings \u2192 preview/change text, captions, visual and input options \u2192 apply \u2192 preferences persist. | Unsupported option/device is labelled unavailable; reset asks confirmation; settings storage failure leaves current-session setting active and explains it may not persist. No permission denial is required for these settings. |\n| J7 | Install, update, and recover from a fault: player retains a coherent playable version. | Install when browser allows \u2192 cache approved release \u2192 play offline \u2192 accept update at launch/menu after save boundary. | Installation prompt may be unavailable/declined without blocking web play; offline uncached assets state the requirement; cache refresh failure retains known-good cache; crash/error boundary offers retry, return to title, and safe recovery. Diagnostics are minimal and consent-gated where required; a player can decline or delete local diagnostic data without losing play. |\n\n## Domain vocabulary and state ownership\n\n| Term | Meaning / owner |\n| --- | --- |\n| Campaign | The fixed first-release sequence from new game through ending; owns completion state. |\n| Scene | One authored playable location: town or dungeon; owns exits, encounter zones, and presentation references. |\n| Quest | Authored objective and state machine that gates campaign progress and rewards. |\n| Party | Player-controlled combat group; owns members' current combat-ready values and progression. Exact party size is an authoring decision. |\n| Encounter | A combat instance created from an authored encounter definition; never persists mid-turn. |\n| Item | Authored definition; an inventory stack/reference is the player-owned instance/count. |\n| Save snapshot | Versioned, validated, atomic representation of durable player state at a safe boundary. |\n| Checkpoint | Authored or system-selected safe snapshot point; it is not a promise to restore arbitrary moment-to-moment state. |\n| Content package | Versioned original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, items, translations, and audiovisual assets delivered together. |\n\n## System relationship map\n\n```text\nContent package \u2500\u2500validates/defines\u2500\u2500> Scene \u2500\u2500starts\u2500\u2500> Encounter\n      \u2502                                  \u2502                  \u2502\n      \u251c\u2500\u2500defines\u2500\u2500> Dialogue \u2500\u2500updates\u2500\u2500> Quest <\u2500\u2500rewards\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n      \u2502                                  \u2502       \u2502\n      \u2514\u2500\u2500defines\u2500\u2500> Items \u2500\u2500held by\u2500\u2500> Inventory \u2502\n                                                 \u2502\nInput + accessibility \u2500\u2500drives\u2500\u2500> Game shell \u2500\u2500> exploration / UI\n                                                 \u2502\nQuest + inventory + party + scene \u2500\u2500snapshot\u2500\u2500> Save / checkpoint\nSave version <\u2500\u2500compatible-with\u2500\u2500 Content package / PWA release\nPWA cache + release workflow \u2500\u2500protect\u2500\u2500> runnable assets and save boundary\nError recovery + minimal diagnostics \u2500\u2500observe\u2500\u2500> shell, persistence, cache\n```\n\n**Cross-domain invariants and lifecycle boundaries**\n\n- A quest transition, reward grant, and save snapshot are ordered: validate\n  transition, apply reward once, then checkpoint; retrying cannot duplicate a\n  reward.\n- An encounter may read party, item, and quest state but changes durable state\n  only after a resolved turn/encounter safe boundary. A crash cannot restore a\n  half-consumed item or half-applied reward.\n- A scene exit is available only when its authored quest predicate is true.\n  Content validation ensures every required predicate, target, reward, and\n  localisation key exists.\n- Settings affect presentation/input immediately but never campaign rules.\n  The same semantic action must be available through supported keyboard,\n  mouse, touch, and gamepad adaptations.\n- Save snapshots record content/schema version and are written atomically.\n  Cache replacement and application migration happen only outside combat and\n  only while a valid fallback save remains intact.\n- The local offline campaign neither needs identity nor sends player state.\n  Any later account is an optional replication boundary, not campaign truth.\n\n## Accepted domain chapters\n\n### 1. Game shell, session, input, and responsive presentation\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Session` moves `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192\nplaying \u2194 paused \u2192 ending \u2192 title`; `InputAction` is mapped per supported input\nmethod; `ViewportProfile` selects responsive layout. Authoring inputs are title\ncopy, control hints, menu routes, and UI layouts. Rules: pause blocks world and\ncombat advancement; focus loss pauses or reaches a safe state; UI action labels\nremain readable and semantic across screen sizes. Dependencies are accessibility,\nrendering, persistence, and content. Outcome is an understandable, controllable\nstart and return path. Edge cases are no existing save, focus loss, rotation,\nunavailable gamepad, unsupported browser feature, and input remap conflict.\n**First-release boundary:** web/PWA keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad\nadaptation; one shared game core. No native-client shell or arbitrary controller\nconfiguration guarantee.\n\n### 2. Exploration, town, dungeon, and campaign content\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Scene` is `unloaded \u2192 entered \u2192 active \u2192 exited`;\n`Exit` is `locked | available | used`; `Interactable` is `available \u2192 used` or\nreusable as authored. Inputs are original tile/layout data, collision shapes,\nspawn points, NPCs, exits, encounter zones, dialogue, and asset references.\nRules: exactly one town and one dungeon form the first campaign; collision and\ngates must leave a completable route. Dependencies are narrative, quests,\ncombat, rendering, and saves. Outcome is readable navigation to the ending.\nEdge cases: blocked exit, empty interaction, absent optional item, and invalid\ncontent reference. **Boundary:** no extra regions, procedural worlds, or shared\nlevels.\n\n### 3. Narrative, quests, onboarding, and ending\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Dialogue` is `available \u2192 shown \u2192 acknowledged`;\n`Quest` is `unavailable \u2192 available \u2192 accepted \u2192 objective-complete \u2192\nclaimed \u2192 completed` (or `failed` only where authored); `TutorialStep` is\n`pending \u2192 presented \u2192 understood`; `Campaign` is `not-started \u2192 active \u2192\ncompleted`. Inputs are original characters, text, localisation keys, objective\npredicates, rewards, and ending sequence. Rules: tutorial teaches a battle and\nsaving before unrestricted progression; required quests cannot be abandoned;\ncompletion is idempotent. Dependencies are scenes, combat, inventory, UI, and\nsaves. Outcomes are clear objectives and a short finish. Edge cases: repeated\nNPC talk, dialogue after completion, missing translation, and an invalid quest\npredicate. **Boundary:** one authored story path; no branching campaign,\nseasonal narrative, or user-authored stories.\n\n### 4. Party combat, encounters, rewards, and balance\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Encounter` is `pending \u2192 active \u2192 player-turn \u2192\nresolution \u2192 won | lost | escaped-if-authored`; `Combatant` is `ready \u2192 acting\n\u2192 resolved \u2192 defeated`; `Reward` is `pending \u2192 granted`. Inputs are party and\nenemy definitions, actions, targeting, encounter placement, reward tables, and\nbalance values. Rules: only legal actions/targets resolve; turn order is visible;\nreward grants once; defeat returns to a safe checkpoint. Dependencies are party,\ninventory, quest transitions, audiovisual feedback, and saves. Outcome is a\nlearnable turn-based first battle and reliable progress. Edge cases: no legal\ntarget, empty item list, invalid action request, pause/focus loss, crash during\nresolution, and stale UI selection. **Boundary:** authored encounters only; no\nmultiplayer, ranked modes, live balance changes, or mid-combat save guarantee.\n\n### 5. Inventory, party progression, and economy\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `InventoryEntry` is `absent \u2192 acquired \u2192 usable |\nequipped \u2192 consumed-if-applicable`; `PartyMember` progresses through authored\nstates; `RewardGrant` is `unclaimed \u2192 applied`. Inputs are item definitions,\ndescriptions, icons, use/equip restrictions, and rewards. Rules: use validates\ntarget and eligibility before mutation; required quest items remain protected;\nduplicate grants are ignored by stable reward ID. Dependencies are combat,\nquests, UI, content validation, and saves. Outcome is meaningful reward use\nwithout dead ends. Edge cases: empty inventory, ineligible target, capacity\nlimit if selected, duplicate reward, and missing item definition. **Boundary:**\nsmall authored set; no crafting, trading, loot boxes, purchases, or destructive\ndiscard flow without approval.\n\n### 6. Save, recovery, and offline persistence\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `SaveSlot` is `empty \u2192 writing \u2192 valid \u2192 loading` or\n`quarantined`; `Checkpoint` is `eligible \u2192 committed`; recovery is `detect \u2192\npreserve \u2192 offer-fallback \u2192 restored | new-game`. Inputs are schema version,\ncampaign/quest/party/inventory/settings state, checkpoint triggers, and\nmigration rules. Rules: validate before replace; retain last known-good data;\nnever overwrite corruption; loading restores only safe scene boundaries; delete\nrequires explicit confirmation. Dependencies are every durable domain, PWA\nstorage, error UX, and release versioning. Outcome is confidence to stop and\nresume. Edge cases: quota/permission denial, malformed data, interrupted write,\nold schema, unavailable local storage, offline launch, and later remote conflict.\n**Boundary:** local durable saves and recovery; remote accounts, sync, cross-\ndevice merge, and cloud deletion policy await approval.\n\n### 7. Accessibility, localisation, and audiovisual feedback\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Preference` is `default \u2192 previewed \u2192 applied \u2192\npersisted`; `LocalePack` is `validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 active`; `FeedbackEvent`\nis emitted by action/scene/combat state. Inputs are accessible labels, text\nstyles, captions, visual settings, translations, original art/audio, and event\nbindings. Rules: settings are understandable and reversible; captions/text do\nnot convey essential information only through sound/colour; missing translation\nfalls back to the approved base language and is logged for content repair.\nDependencies are UI, content packaging, input, and storage. Outcome is readable,\ncontrollable play with clear feedback. Edge cases: unsupported preference,\nstorage failure, missing locale key, muted audio, contrast conflict, and narrow\nviewport. **Boundary:** the settings categories named in the brief and a\nlanguage-content pipeline; exact languages, remapping depth, ratings, and audio\nproduction scope remain decisions.\n\n### 8. PWA delivery, release safety, diagnostics, and quality operations\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Release` is `built \u2192 validated \u2192 published \u2192 cached \u2192\nsuperseded`; `Cache` is `installing \u2192 ready \u2192 retained | replaced`; `Fault` is\n`caught \u2192 player-recovered \u2192 optionally-reported`. Inputs are asset manifests,\ncontent/save compatibility declarations, service-worker policy, error messages,\nminimal diagnostic schema, and test matrices. Rules: an update activates at a\ntitle/menu safe boundary after a confirmed save; failed refresh retains a\nknown-good cache; diagnostics minimise data and respect consent; supported\nbrowser/device/network and performance thresholds must be agreed before release\nacceptance. Dependencies are all packaged content, persistence, shell, privacy,\nand quality checks. Outcome is safe installation, offline continuation, update,\nand error recovery. Edge cases: declined install, first offline visit, stale\ncache, asset fetch failure, crash loop, diagnostics denial/deletion, and storage\npressure. **Boundary:** installable web/PWA and minimal crash recovery only; no\nlive event operation, account support desk, analytics programme, or paid-service\nSLO until approved.\n\n## Capability parity and intentional differences\n\n| Capability | Responsive web | Installed PWA | Shared rule |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Campaign, combat, inventory, quests, settings, saves | Required | Required | Same content, rules, save schema, and accessible semantic actions. |\n| Input | Keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad | Same where device/browser exposes it | Input adapters map to one action vocabulary. |\n| Responsive presentation | Required on phone, tablet, desktop | Required on phone, tablet, desktop | Layout adapts; no gameplay advantage by surface. |\n| Offline play/assets | May work once cached | Primary expected offline route once cached | First visit needs assets; saves remain local and recoverable. |\n| Installation | Browser page can offer it where supported | Installable experience | Declining/unavailable install never blocks web play. |\n| Updates | Cache refresh at safe boundary | Cache refresh at safe boundary | Never swap content/version during unresolved combat or save write. |\n\n## Prioritised feature catalogue and slices\n\n| Priority | Feature | User outcome / journey | Slice |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| P0 | Shell, title/new game, pause, responsive input/presentation | Start and control the game (J1). | First release |\n| P0 | One town, one dungeon, original content packaging and validation | Traverse one completable campaign (J3). | First release |\n| P0 | Dialogue, quest state, onboarding, short ending | Understand and complete story progress (J1\u2013J3). | First release |\n| P0 | Party turn-based combat, tutorial encounter, rewards | Finish first battle and understand the loop (J2). | First release |\n| P0 | Inventory/progression UI and safe item rules | Use earned rewards without dead ends (J4). | First release |\n| P0 | Atomic local save/load, checkpoints, corruption recovery, save deletion | Stop, resume, and recover confirmed progress (J5). | First release |\n| P0 | Settings: accessible controls/text/captions/visuals; localisation pipeline | Play comfortably and read core UI (J1, J6). | First release |\n| P0 | Web/PWA caching, install path, update safety, error recovery | Keep a stable offline-capable version (J7). | First release |\n| P0 | Original art/audio feedback and quality validation | Receive clear, original feedback on supported targets (J2, J6). | First release |\n| P1 | Additional locales, refined remapping, content expansion | Broader comfort and longer campaign. | Later, after languages/content scope is approved |\n| P1 | Optional account-linked backup/sync | Recover across devices with explicit conflict choices. | Later, approval required |\n| P1 | Multiplayer, player safety, moderation, support and live operations | Play safely with others. | Later, approval required; not implied by single-player game |\n| P2 | Live events/seasonal content; player-created/shared content | Receive or create continuing content. | Deferred |\n| P2 | Advanced analytics/monetisation, purchases, catalogue, entitlements/refunds | Optional commercial/personalised experience. | Deferred; commerce approval required |\n\nThe P0 set deliberately forms a complete useful journey: J1 starts and teaches,\nJ2 proves the core loop, J3 reaches the ending, J4 supports rewards, J5 makes\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"ls projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R001{7,8,9}.md projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md 2>&1; sed -n '1,120p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0008.md; sed -n '1,130p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nls: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md: No such file or directory\nls: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md: No such file or directory\nls: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md: No such file or directory\nls: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md: No such file or directory\n---\ntask_id: B0008\nsequence: 11\ntitle: Author campaign integration and original-content contracts\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate only `../runbooks/R0017.md` through `../runbooks/R0020.md` from the\nassigned SHARD-02 catalogue contracts, after their listed R0013\u2013R0016\npredecessors. Preserve GATE-0004 and the human provenance review.\n\n## Context packet\n\nRead `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, the B0008 and assigned R manifest records,\n`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n`../specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content`\nthrough `#5-inventory-party-progression-and-economy`, and\n`../specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas`.\nUse `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` and F014 provenance/asset rules.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `../runbooks/R0017.md` \u2014 IMP-0017.\n- `../runbooks/R0018.md` \u2014 IMP-0018.\n- `../runbooks/R0019.md` \u2014 IMP-0019.\n- `../runbooks/R0020.md` \u2014 IMP-0020.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nBefore writing, confirm no accepted path will be overwritten. Match each R\nfront matter, requirement IDs, dependencies, ownership, canonical provenance,\nfactory stages, and asset metadata to the manifest. Every R includes standard\nsections, `## Verification`, and `## Asset assessment`; asset-required R0018\nmust name only its reserved stable asset IDs and prohibit creation in authoring.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nCheckpoint only validated assigned files. Retain R0017\u2013R0020 on failure and\nrepair only the failing output before rerunning the structural validator through\nB0008; never treat implementation gates as authoring approval.\n\n## Collision protection\n\nCheck manifest and filesystem ownership before each write. Stop for duplicate\nIDs/paths, dependency/provenance mismatch, missing asset assessment, or a\nconflict with accepted work; do not renumber or reallocate.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop after these four outputs. Do not author a UI/PWA contract, allocate more\nwork, or create the reserved product assets.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Exactly R0017 through R0020 are created, each mapping only to its assigned\n  `IMP-*` record.\n- Every generated R file has valid Supervisor metadata, canonical provenance,\n  requirement links, dependency-correct ownership, verification, and an\n  explicit asset/audio assessment.\n- R0018 reserves its manifest-defined stable asset IDs and records the human\n  provenance review without creating product assets during authoring.\n- The structural validator succeeds through B0008 before this B task is\n  accepted, without overwriting an accepted contract.\n---\ntask_id: R0013\nsequence: 13\ntitle: Define exploration scene and exit transition contract\ndependencies: R0004,R0005\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0013\nauthoring_batch: B0007\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; content-neutral scene and transition contracts.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the shared, content-neutral scene, exit, collision, and interaction\ntransition contract that preserves a completable route. This task owns rules\nand envelopes only, not maps, presentation, or authored campaign content.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0004 provides immutable state, commands, events, and invariants; R0005\nprovides the content schema and reference validator. Both remain their owners.\nGATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete scene, locale, map, and\ncontent shapes; it does not defer this contract's authoring.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/core/campaign/scene*` and `tests/core/campaign/scene*`.\n- The scene and exit envelope, including stable scene/exit/interaction IDs.\n- Shared scene-transition commands and route-graph validation boundary.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nModel scene entry, available exits, collision/interaction eligibility, and\ntransition outcomes as deterministic shared-core data. Validate references,\nthe expected revision, current-scene membership, predicate eligibility, and\ndestination reachability before mutating state. An invalid, blocked, stale, or\nunknown exit returns a typed rejection and leaves state unchanged. A validated\nroute graph must identify a start-to-completion path without adding concrete\nmap geometry or authored locations.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nResponsive web and installed PWA adapters submit the same scene commands and\nrender returned state/events. They may translate input or visual collision\nsignals into commands but cannot interpret or mutate campaign transitions.\nRendering, navigation layout, browser history, cache lifecycle, and PWA\ninstallation are outside this shared-core contract.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not create UI, maps, extra regions, procedural worlds, authored locations,\ndialogue, assets, audio, input handling, browser navigation, persistence\ndrivers, or concrete content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: scene envelopes and validation do not need\nvisual or source assets. Do not create or reserve incidental maps, tiles,\nsprites, icons, textures, illustrations, fonts, or other product assets;\n`asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Audio assessment\n\n`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract neither selects nor triggers\nmusic or sound effects. Keep audio IDs, brief, and style version blank; do not\ncreate incidental cues.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Use deterministic fixtures to show invalid exits, unknown references, stale\n  commands, and blocked predicates leave the exact prior state unchanged.\n- Validate a minimal abstract route graph and reject an unreachable destination\n  or invalid exit reference without introducing authored maps or locations.\n- Compare metadata, ownership, requirements, provenance, and dependencies with\n  IMP-0013 and the R0013 manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain fixture output for rejected and legal transitions, route-graph validator\nresults, the ownership comparison, and the recorded unresolved GATE-0004.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Scene, exit, collision, and interaction transitions are shared-core,\n  deterministic, reference-checked, and content-neutral.\n- Invalid exits and references do not mutate state, and route validation proves\n  a completable abstract path.\n- GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content implementation; no UI,\n  authored map, visual asset, or audio work is introduced.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The four assigned paths are absent and unclaimed. I\u2019ve matched their metadata, dependencies, requirements, asset reservation, and gate constraints to the manifest/catalogue; I\u2019m now writing only those four contracts.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Verified B0008 allocation and collision protection before authoring.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0008.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"runbooks/F014.md\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Runbook contracts are the requested documentation artifact; no README update is needed.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Domain-only shared contracts; no browser spec is appropriate.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..128dec9061cedec05ce7de6cedd0c75144a4a125\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0017\n+sequence: 17\n+title: Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0017\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored campaign expression; integration rules only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon\n+route, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected\n+inventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration\n+rules, not authored story or presentation.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015\n+owns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This\n+contract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.\n+- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,\n+  and the campaign-completion command.\n+- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Accept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final\n+state: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required\n+encounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate\n+expected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits\n+one stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request\n+returns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending\n+effects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed\n+rejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render\n+its state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,\n+and installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,\n+audio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.\n+Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration\n+contract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,\n+portraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or\n+mix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending\n+  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.\n+- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests\n+  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to\n+  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the\n+manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.\n+- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and\n+  reward grants cannot occur.\n+- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain\n+  outside this contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5524db86603e1fcfae58b95d11826af317a61b38\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0018\n+sequence: 18\n+title: Define original campaign content-package and provenance assembly\n+dependencies: R0005,R0011,R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0018\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: required\n+asset_ids: ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS\n+asset_brief: Reserve original campaign asset groups for later approved implementation; authoring creates no asset.\n+visual_style_version: unselected-gate-0004\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the\n+town, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain\n+contracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;\n+do not create product expression during authoring.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the\n+provenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013\u2013R0016\n+provide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This\n+contract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.\n+GATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of\n+concrete authored content; neither is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and\n+  `tests/content/campaign*`.\n+- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest\n+  entries for the reserved asset groups.\n+- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Assemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the\n+campaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must\n+have a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as\n+defined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,\n+whose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is\n+recorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.\n+The package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define\n+new gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks\n+cannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.\n+Rendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior\n+remain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,\n+dialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.\n+Do not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve\n+GATE-0004 or the human review.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They\n+appear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of\n+truth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,\n+visual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under\n+`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before\n+admission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit\n+human creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated\n+by this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and\n+style version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character\n+  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.\n+- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a\n+  package not marked ready after human review is rejected before admission.\n+- Check that the three reserved IDs, asset brief, and style placeholder match\n+  IMP-0018 and the manifest, with no asset created; retain GATE-0004 and the\n+  recorded human provenance-review requirement.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain package-validator results, rejected provenance fixtures, the synthetic\n+human-review disposition, asset-reservation comparison, and both gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The versioned package resolves only validated, stable campaign references.\n+- Every expressive entry requires complete provenance and a recorded human\n+  creative-review disposition before admission.\n+- Only the three manifest-defined asset IDs are reserved; no product asset,\n+  copied expression, or creative/legal approval is created or claimed.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f5e8b01a9832de3d4e34d0d94d13fdd7966cd52b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0019\n+sequence: 19\n+title: Add campaign domain invariant and negative-fixture coverage\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0019\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; deterministic invalid-state fixtures only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Add deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for\n+the SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,\n+blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without\n+introducing concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter\n+and reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns\n+fixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state\n+rules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.\n+- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.\n+- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,\n+reward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;\n+stale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a\n+stable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never\n+mutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid\n+abstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep\n+fixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+These are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,\n+responsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,\n+real player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete\n+content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require\n+no product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+textures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect\n+trigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product\n+cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including\n+  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.\n+- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract\n+  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.\n+- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against\n+  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run\n+comparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected\n+  coverage and does not mutate state.\n+- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate\n+  grants are repeat-safe.\n+- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,\n+  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a972ced7298533227a772ac88cd7240691489440\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0020\n+sequence: 20\n+title: Document SHARD-02 ownership, gates, and handoff boundaries\n+dependencies: R0017,R0018,R0019\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0012\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership,specification/02-feature-model.md#capability-parity-and-intentional-differences\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0020\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; documentation and SHARD-03 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,\n+asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a\n+developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly\n+and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This\n+handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion\n+resolves GATE-0004 or human review.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.\n+- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.\n+- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,\n+encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content\n+package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks\n+concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance\n+review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or\n+documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,\n+accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the\n+shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume\n+the same campaign rules and validated content, but their UI, input adapters,\n+cache/install/update lifecycle, and release delivery are not SHARD-02 work.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement UI, PWA delivery, browser tests, rendering, input mappings,\n+asset production, audio, release claims, product changes, or gate approvals.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this documentation creates no visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve any product asset; `asset_ids` remains\n+blank. R0018 remains the sole owner of its reserved campaign asset IDs.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no cue, playback behavior, or mix belongs\n+to this documentation handoff. Keep audio metadata blank/default and create no\n+audio asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Cross-check the ownership index against IMP-0013 through IMP-0020 and\n+  R0013\u2013R0019, confirming every shared domain has one stated owner/boundary.\n+- Confirm GATE-0004, human provenance review, R0018 asset reservation, and the\n+  SHARD-03 UI/PWA boundary are explicit and unresolved where required.\n+- Compare metadata, requirement IDs, dependencies, provenance, and ownership\n+  with IMP-0020 and the manifest without making release-readiness claims.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the ownership cross-check, gate/provenance review record, SHARD-03\n+handoff review, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The documentation assigns SHARD-02 domain ownership and its interfaces\n+  without claiming UI or PWA implementation ownership.\n+- GATE-0004, the human provenance review, and R0018 asset-reservation boundary\n+  are explicit and unresolved.\n+- SHARD-03 receives a clear documented handoff for UI, input, accessibility,\n+  responsive web, and installed-PWA responsibilities.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..128dec9061cedec05ce7de6cedd0c75144a4a125\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0017\n+sequence: 17\n+title: Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0017\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored campaign expression; integration rules only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon\n+route, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected\n+inventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration\n+rules, not authored story or presentation.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015\n+owns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This\n+contract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.\n+- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,\n+  and the campaign-completion command.\n+- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Accept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final\n+state: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required\n+encounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate\n+expected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits\n+one stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request\n+returns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending\n+effects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed\n+rejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render\n+its state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,\n+and installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,\n+audio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.\n+Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration\n+contract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,\n+portraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or\n+mix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending\n+  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.\n+- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests\n+  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to\n+  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the\n+manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.\n+- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and\n+  reward grants cannot occur.\n+- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain\n+  outside this contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5524db86603e1fcfae58b95d11826af317a61b38\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0018\n+sequence: 18\n+title: Define original campaign content-package and provenance assembly\n+dependencies: R0005,R0011,R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0018\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: required\n+asset_ids: ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS\n+asset_brief: Reserve original campaign asset groups for later approved implementation; authoring creates no asset.\n+visual_style_version: unselected-gate-0004\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the\n+town, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain\n+contracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;\n+do not create product expression during authoring.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the\n+provenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013\u2013R0016\n+provide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This\n+contract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.\n+GATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of\n+concrete authored content; neither is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and\n+  `tests/content/campaign*`.\n+- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest\n+  entries for the reserved asset groups.\n+- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Assemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the\n+campaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must\n+have a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as\n+defined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,\n+whose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is\n+recorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.\n+The package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define\n+new gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks\n+cannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.\n+Rendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior\n+remain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,\n+dialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.\n+Do not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve\n+GATE-0004 or the human review.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They\n+appear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of\n+truth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,\n+visual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under\n+`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before\n+admission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit\n+human creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated\n+by this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and\n+style version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character\n+  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.\n+- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a\n+  package not marked ready after human review is rejected before admission.\n+- Check that the three reserved IDs, asset brief, and style placeholder match\n+  IMP-0018 and the manifest, with no asset created; retain GATE-0004 and the\n+  recorded human provenance-review requirement.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain package-validator results, rejected provenance fixtures, the synthetic\n+human-review disposition, asset-reservation comparison, and both gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The versioned package resolves only validated, stable campaign references.\n+- Every expressive entry requires complete provenance and a recorded human\n+  creative-review disposition before admission.\n+- Only the three manifest-defined asset IDs are reserved; no product asset,\n+  copied expression, or creative/legal approval is created or claimed.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f5e8b01a9832de3d4e34d0d94d13fdd7966cd52b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0019\n+sequence: 19\n+title: Add campaign domain invariant and negative-fixture coverage\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0019\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; deterministic invalid-state fixtures only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Add deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for\n+the SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,\n+blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without\n+introducing concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter\n+and reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns\n+fixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state\n+rules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.\n+- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.\n+- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,\n+reward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;\n+stale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a\n+stable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never\n+mutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid\n+abstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep\n+fixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+These are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,\n+responsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,\n+real player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete\n+content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require\n+no product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+textures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect\n+trigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product\n+cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including\n+  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.\n+- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract\n+  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.\n+- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against\n+  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run\n+comparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected\n+  coverage and does not mutate state.\n+- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate\n+  grants are repeat-safe.\n+- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,\n+  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a972ced7298533227a772ac88cd7240691489440\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0020\n+sequence: 20\n+title: Document SHARD-02 ownership, gates, and handoff boundaries\n+dependencies: R0017,R0018,R0019\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0012\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership,specification/02-feature-model.md#capability-parity-and-intentional-differences\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0020\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; documentation and SHARD-03 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,\n+asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a\n+developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly\n+and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This\n+handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion\n+resolves GATE-0004 or human review.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.\n+- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.\n+- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,\n+encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content\n+package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks\n+concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance\n+review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or\n+documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,\n+accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the\n+shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume\n+the same campaign rules and validated content, but their UI, input adapters,\n+cache/install/update lifecycle, and release delivery are not SHARD-02 work.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement UI, PWA delivery, browser tests, rendering, input mappings,\n+asset production, audio, release claims, product changes, or gate approvals.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this documentation creates no visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve any product asset; `asset_ids` remains\n+blank. R0018 remains the sole owner of its reserved campaign asset IDs.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no cue, playback behavior, or mix belongs\n+to this documentation handoff. Keep audio metadata blank/default and create no\n+audio asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Cross-check the ownership index against IMP-0013 through IMP-0020 and\n+  R0013\u2013R0019, confirming every shared domain has one stated owner/boundary.\n+- Confirm GATE-0004, human provenance review, R0018 asset reservation, and the\n+  SHARD-03 UI/PWA boundary are explicit and unresolved where required.\n+- Compare metadata, requirement IDs, dependencies, provenance, and ownership\n+  with IMP-0020 and the manifest without making release-readiness claims.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the ownership cross-check, gate/provenance review record, SHARD-03\n+handoff review, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The documentation assigns SHARD-02 domain ownership and its interfaces\n+  without claiming UI or PWA implementation ownership.\n+- GATE-0004, the human provenance review, and R0018 asset-reservation boundary\n+  are explicit and unresolved.\n+- SHARD-03 receives a clear documented handoff for UI, input, accessibility,\n+  responsive web, and installed-PWA responsibilities.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0008 && git diff --check && git status --short' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nRunbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\ncanonical specification chapters: 13\nspecification provenance links: 39\ncatalogue contracts: 20 (IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004, IMP-0005, IMP-0006, IMP-0007, IMP-0008, IMP-0009, IMP-0010, IMP-0011, IMP-0012, IMP-0013, IMP-0014, IMP-0015, IMP-0016, IMP-0017, IMP-0018, IMP-0019, IMP-0020)\nmanifest contracts: 20 (R0001, R0002, R0003, R0004, R0005, R0006, R0007, R0008, R0009, R0010, R0011, R0012, R0013, R0014, R0015, R0016, R0017, R0018, R0019, R0020)\nR files missing: 0\nblocked contracts: 0\nunverified contracts: 0\nunallocated catalogue contracts: 0\nreserved asset IDs: 3 (ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN)\nbrowser test paths: 0\n M README.md\n m supervisor\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/\n?? runbooks/.supervisor-children/\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..128dec9061cedec05ce7de6cedd0c75144a4a125\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0017\n+sequence: 17\n+title: Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0017\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored campaign expression; integration rules only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon\n+route, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected\n+inventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration\n+rules, not authored story or presentation.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015\n+owns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This\n+contract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.\n+- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,\n+  and the campaign-completion command.\n+- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Accept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final\n+state: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required\n+encounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate\n+expected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits\n+one stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request\n+returns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending\n+effects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed\n+rejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render\n+its state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,\n+and installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,\n+audio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.\n+Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration\n+contract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,\n+portraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or\n+mix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending\n+  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.\n+- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests\n+  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to\n+  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the\n+manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.\n+- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and\n+  reward grants cannot occur.\n+- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain\n+  outside this contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5524db86603e1fcfae58b95d11826af317a61b38\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0018\n+sequence: 18\n+title: Define original campaign content-package and provenance assembly\n+dependencies: R0005,R0011,R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0018\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: required\n+asset_ids: ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS\n+asset_brief: Reserve original campaign asset groups for later approved implementation; authoring creates no asset.\n+visual_style_version: unselected-gate-0004\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the\n+town, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain\n+contracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;\n+do not create product expression during authoring.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the\n+provenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013\u2013R0016\n+provide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This\n+contract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.\n+GATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of\n+concrete authored content; neither is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and\n+  `tests/content/campaign*`.\n+- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest\n+  entries for the reserved asset groups.\n+- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Assemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the\n+campaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must\n+have a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as\n+defined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,\n+whose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is\n+recorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.\n+The package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define\n+new gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks\n+cannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.\n+Rendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior\n+remain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,\n+dialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.\n+Do not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve\n+GATE-0004 or the human review.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They\n+appear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of\n+truth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,\n+visual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under\n+`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before\n+admission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit\n+human creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated\n+by this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and\n+style version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character\n+  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.\n+- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a\n+  package not marked ready after human review is rejected before admission.\n+- Check that the three reserved IDs, asset brief, and style placeholder match\n+  IMP-0018 and the manifest, with no asset created; retain GATE-0004 and the\n+  recorded human provenance-review requirement.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain package-validator results, rejected provenance fixtures, the synthetic\n+human-review disposition, asset-reservation comparison, and both gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The versioned package resolves only validated, stable campaign references.\n+- Every expressive entry requires complete provenance and a recorded human\n+  creative-review disposition before admission.\n+- Only the three manifest-defined asset IDs are reserved; no product asset,\n+  copied expression, or creative/legal approval is created or claimed.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f5e8b01a9832de3d4e34d0d94d13fdd7966cd52b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0019\n+sequence: 19\n+title: Add campaign domain invariant and negative-fixture coverage\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0019\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; deterministic invalid-state fixtures only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Add deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for\n+the SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,\n+blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without\n+introducing concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter\n+and reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns\n+fixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state\n+rules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.\n+- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.\n+- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,\n+reward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;\n+stale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a\n+stable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never\n+mutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid\n+abstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep\n+fixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+These are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,\n+responsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,\n+real player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete\n+content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require\n+no product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+textures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect\n+trigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product\n+cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including\n+  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.\n+- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract\n+  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.\n+- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against\n+  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run\n+comparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected\n+  coverage and does not mutate state.\n+- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate\n+  grants are repeat-safe.\n+- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,\n+  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a972ced7298533227a772ac88cd7240691489440\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0020\n+sequence: 20\n+title: Document SHARD-02 ownership, gates, and handoff boundaries\n+dependencies: R0017,R0018,R0019\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0012\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership,specification/02-feature-model.md#capability-parity-and-intentional-differences\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0020\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; documentation and SHARD-03 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,\n+asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a\n+developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly\n+and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This\n+handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion\n+resolves GATE-0004 or human review.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.\n+- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.\n+- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,\n+encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content\n+package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks\n+concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance\n+review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or\n+documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,\n+accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the\n+shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume\n+the same campaign rules and validated content, but their UI, input adapters,\n+cache/install/update lifecycle, and release delivery are not SHARD-02 work.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement UI, PWA delivery, browser tests, rendering, input mappings,\n+asset production, audio, release claims, product changes, or gate approvals.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this documentation creates no visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve any product asset; `asset_ids` remains\n+blank. R0018 remains the sole owner of its reserved campaign asset IDs.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no cue, playback behavior, or mix belongs\n+to this documentation handoff. Keep audio metadata blank/default and create no\n+audio asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Cross-check the ownership index against IMP-0013 through IMP-0020 and\n+  R0013\u2013R0019, confirming every shared domain has one stated owner/boundary.\n+- Confirm GATE-0004, human provenance review, R0018 asset reservation, and the\n+  SHARD-03 UI/PWA boundary are explicit and unresolved where required.\n+- Compare metadata, requirement IDs, dependencies, provenance, and ownership\n+  with IMP-0020 and the manifest without making release-readiness claims.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the ownership cross-check, gate/provenance review record, SHARD-03\n+handoff review, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The documentation assigns SHARD-02 domain ownership and its interfaces\n+  without claiming UI or PWA implementation ownership.\n+- GATE-0004, the human provenance review, and R0018 asset-reservation boundary\n+  are explicit and unresolved.\n+- SHARD-03 receives a clear documented handoff for UI, input, accessibility,\n+  responsive web, and installed-PWA responsibilities.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created only the four assigned SHARD-02 implementation-runbook contracts. Structural validation through B0008 passes, including the R0018 asset reservations and retained gate/provenance requirements.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\"],\"test_result\":\"PASS: python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0008 (20 manifest contracts; 0 missing R files; 0 unverified contracts; reserved asset IDs match R0018). PASS: git diff --check.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Confirmed R0017\u2013R0020 did not exist before authoring; consulted the B0008 allocation, manifest, catalogue, feature model, F014 requirements, and predecessor contracts.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"Structural quality gate completed successfully through B0008; git diff --check completed successfully.\",\"browser_log\":\"No browser behavior or UI/PWA implementation is owned by these shared/domain documentation contracts.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Exactly R0017 through R0020 are created, each mapping only to its assigned `IMP-*` record.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created R0017\u2192IMP-0017, R0018\u2192IMP-0018, R0019\u2192IMP-0019, and R0020\u2192IMP-0020 only. The structural validator reports 20 ordered manifest contracts, 0 missing R files, and 0 unallocated catalogue contracts.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Every generated R file has valid Supervisor metadata, canonical provenance, requirement links, dependency-correct ownership, verification, and an explicit asset/audio assessment.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"All four files declare task, sequence, requirements, dependencies, source specifications/catalogue IDs, batch, stages, asset and audio metadata, and include Verification, Asset assessment, and Audio assessment sections. Validator passed through B0008.\"},{\"criterion\":\"R0018 reserves its manifest-defined stable asset IDs and records the human provenance review without creating product assets during authoring.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"R0018 reserves ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON, and ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS exactly, retains visual_style_version unselected-gate-0004, and explicitly requires human creative/provenance review while prohibiting asset creation.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The structural validator succeeds through B0008 before this B task is accepted, without overwriting an accepted contract.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"`python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0008` exited 0. Paths were confirmed absent before creation; no accepted R contract was overwritten.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0008.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\",\"runbooks/F014.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0013.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0016.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\"],\"summary\":\"The requested implementation-runbook contracts are the documentation deliverable. No README, plan, or ADR was changed because the task explicitly limited changes to the four assigned R-series files.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: each assigned IMP record targets shared/domain documentation or deterministic fixtures and explicitly excludes UI/PWA behavior; no task-specific Playwright specification changed.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..128dec9061cedec05ce7de6cedd0c75144a4a125\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0017\n+sequence: 17\n+title: Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0017\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored campaign expression; integration rules only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon\n+route, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected\n+inventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration\n+rules, not authored story or presentation.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015\n+owns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This\n+contract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.\n+- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,\n+  and the campaign-completion command.\n+- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Accept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final\n+state: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required\n+encounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate\n+expected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits\n+one stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request\n+returns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending\n+effects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed\n+rejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render\n+its state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,\n+and installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,\n+audio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.\n+Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration\n+contract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,\n+portraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or\n+mix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending\n+  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.\n+- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests\n+  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to\n+  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the\n+manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.\n+- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and\n+  reward grants cannot occur.\n+- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain\n+  outside this contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5524db86603e1fcfae58b95d11826af317a61b38\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0018\n+sequence: 18\n+title: Define original campaign content-package and provenance assembly\n+dependencies: R0005,R0011,R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0018\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: required\n+asset_ids: ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS\n+asset_brief: Reserve original campaign asset groups for later approved implementation; authoring creates no asset.\n+visual_style_version: unselected-gate-0004\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the\n+town, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain\n+contracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;\n+do not create product expression during authoring.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the\n+provenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013\u2013R0016\n+provide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This\n+contract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.\n+GATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of\n+concrete authored content; neither is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and\n+  `tests/content/campaign*`.\n+- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest\n+  entries for the reserved asset groups.\n+- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Assemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the\n+campaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must\n+have a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as\n+defined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,\n+whose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is\n+recorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.\n+The package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define\n+new gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks\n+cannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.\n+Rendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior\n+remain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,\n+dialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.\n+Do not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve\n+GATE-0004 or the human review.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They\n+appear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of\n+truth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,\n+visual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under\n+`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before\n+admission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit\n+human creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated\n+by this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and\n+style version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character\n+  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.\n+- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a\n+  package not marked ready after human review is rejected before admission.\n+- Check that the three reserved IDs, asset brief, and style placeholder match\n+  IMP-0018 and the manifest, with no asset created; retain GATE-0004 and the\n+  recorded human provenance-review requirement.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain package-validator results, rejected provenance fixtures, the synthetic\n+human-review disposition, asset-reservation comparison, and both gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The versioned package resolves only validated, stable campaign references.\n+- Every expressive entry requires complete provenance and a recorded human\n+  creative-review disposition before admission.\n+- Only the three manifest-defined asset IDs are reserved; no product asset,\n+  copied expression, or creative/legal approval is created or claimed.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f5e8b01a9832de3d4e34d0d94d13fdd7966cd52b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0019\n+sequence: 19\n+title: Add campaign domain invariant and negative-fixture coverage\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0019\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; deterministic invalid-state fixtures only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Add deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for\n+the SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,\n+blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without\n+introducing concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter\n+and reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns\n+fixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state\n+rules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.\n+- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.\n+- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,\n+reward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;\n+stale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a\n+stable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never\n+mutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid\n+abstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep\n+fixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+These are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,\n+responsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,\n+real player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete\n+content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require\n+no product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+textures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect\n+trigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product\n+cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including\n+  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.\n+- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract\n+  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.\n+- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against\n+  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run\n+comparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected\n+  coverage and does not mutate state.\n+- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate\n+  grants are repeat-safe.\n+- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,\n+  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a972ced7298533227a772ac88cd7240691489440\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0020\n+sequence: 20\n+title: Document SHARD-02 ownership, gates, and handoff boundaries\n+dependencies: R0017,R0018,R0019\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0012\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership,specification/02-feature-model.md#capability-parity-and-intentional-differences\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0020\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; documentation and SHARD-03 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,\n+asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a\n+developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly\n+and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This\n+handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion\n+resolves GATE-0004 or human review.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.\n+- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.\n+- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,\n+encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content\n+package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks\n+concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance\n+review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or\n+documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,\n+accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the\n+shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume\n+the same campaign rules and validated content, but their UI, input adapters,\n+cache/install/update lifecycle, and release delivery are not SHARD-02 work.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement UI, PWA delivery, browser tests, rendering, input mappings,\n+asset production, audio, release claims, product changes, or gate approvals.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this documentation creates no visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve any product asset; `asset_ids` remains\n+blank. R0018 remains the sole owner of its reserved campaign asset IDs.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no cue, playback behavior, or mix belongs\n+to this documentation handoff. Keep audio metadata blank/default and create no\n+audio asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Cross-check the ownership index against IMP-0013 through IMP-0020 and\n+  R0013\u2013R0019, confirming every shared domain has one stated owner/boundary.\n+- Confirm GATE-0004, human provenance review, R0018 asset reservation, and the\n+  SHARD-03 UI/PWA boundary are explicit and unresolved where required.\n+- Compare metadata, requirement IDs, dependencies, provenance, and ownership\n+  with IMP-0020 and the manifest without making release-readiness claims.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the ownership cross-check, gate/provenance review record, SHARD-03\n+handoff review, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The documentation assigns SHARD-02 domain ownership and its interfaces\n+  without claiming UI or PWA implementation ownership.\n+- GATE-0004, the human provenance review, and R0018 asset-reservation boundary\n+  are explicit and unresolved.\n+- SHARD-03 receives a clear documented handoff for UI, input, accessibility,\n+  responsive web, and installed-PWA responsibilities.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created only R0017\u2013R0020 for B0008; structural validation passes through B0008.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\"],\"test_result\":\"PASS: python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0008. PASS: git diff --check.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Confirmed assigned paths were absent, then matched contracts to B0008, manifest, catalogue, specifications, F014, and predecessor runbooks.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"Validator: 0 missing R files, 0 unverified contracts; 3 reserved R0018 asset IDs.\",\"browser_log\":\"No browser/UI/PWA scope is owned by these contracts.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Exactly R0017 through R0020 are created, each mapping only to its assigned `IMP-*` record.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created R0017\u2192IMP-0017, R0018\u2192IMP-0018, R0019\u2192IMP-0019, and R0020\u2192IMP-0020 only; validator reports no missing or unallocated contracts.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Every generated R file has valid Supervisor metadata, canonical provenance, requirement links, dependency-correct ownership, verification, and an explicit asset/audio assessment.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"All four files include required metadata, canonical links, requirement IDs, dependencies, ownership, Verification, Asset assessment, and Audio assessment; validator passes.\"},{\"criterion\":\"R0018 reserves its manifest-defined stable asset IDs and records the human provenance review without creating product assets during authoring.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"R0018 reserves ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON, and ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS, requires human review, and prohibits asset creation.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The structural validator succeeds through B0008 before this B task is accepted, without overwriting an accepted contract.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Validator exited 0 through B0008. All four target paths were confirmed absent before creation.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0008.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\",\"runbooks/F014.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\"],\"summary\":\"The requested R-series contracts are the documentation deliverable; no README/plan update was needed because scope was limited to these four files.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: shared/domain contracts explicitly exclude UI and PWA behavior, so no Playwright spec changed.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..128dec9061cedec05ce7de6cedd0c75144a4a125\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0017.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0017\n+sequence: 17\n+title: Specify campaign progression and safe ending integration\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0017\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No authored campaign expression; integration rules only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the shared-core integration that joins the abstract town-to-dungeon\n+route, required quest/tutorial progress, encounter rewards, and protected\n+inventory into one safely completable campaign ending. It owns integration\n+rules, not authored story or presentation.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 owns scene transitions, R0014 owns quest and tutorial transitions, R0015\n+owns encounter/reward resolution, and R0016 owns inventory/party safety. This\n+contract composes their public outcomes without transferring their ownership.\n+GATE-0004 remains an implementation gate for concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/campaign/progression*` and `tests/core/campaign/progression*`.\n+- Campaign route graph, integration checkpoints, completion-state envelope,\n+  and the campaign-completion command.\n+- Cross-domain ordering rules from validated route through ending completion.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Accept completion only when a validated route has reached the authorised final\n+state: legal scene transition, required quest progression, resolved required\n+encounter/reward outcome, and protected-item predicates must all hold. Validate\n+expected revision and completion eligibility before mutation. Completion emits\n+one stable result and is idempotent: a duplicate or stale completion request\n+returns the recorded result without replaying grants, transitions, or ending\n+effects. Invalid, blocked, or dead-end routes preserve state with typed\n+rejection; optional rewards cannot be completion prerequisites.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed-PWA adapters submit the same completion command and render\n+its state/event. Ending UI, navigation, animation, cache updates, persistence,\n+and installation lifecycle are outside this shared-core contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author town/dungeon maps, characters, dialogue, ending text, assets,\n+audio, UI, extra regions, branching stories, remote content, or save drivers.\n+Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is a content-neutral integration\n+contract. Do not create or reserve maps, illustrations, sprites, textures,\n+portraits, icons, fonts, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: the contract does not select, trigger, or\n+mix music or sound effects. Keep all audio fields blank/default and do not\n+create incidental cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic abstract fixtures to prove exactly one start-to-ending\n+  route is reachable only after required cross-domain predicates hold.\n+- Prove blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate completion requests\n+  preserve state or return the recorded completion result; no reward repeats.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, ownership, provenance, and dependencies to\n+  IMP-0017 and its manifest allocation; retain GATE-0004 explicitly.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain reachability output, rejection and duplicate-completion fixtures, the\n+manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- One validated abstract route reaches campaign completion without a dead end.\n+- Ending completion is revision-checked and idempotent; duplicate effects and\n+  reward grants cannot occur.\n+- Concrete authored content, UI, assets, audio, and GATE-0004 approval remain\n+  outside this contract.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5524db86603e1fcfae58b95d11826af317a61b38\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0018.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0018\n+sequence: 18\n+title: Define original campaign content-package and provenance assembly\n+dependencies: R0005,R0011,R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#3-narrative-quests-onboarding-and-ending,specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0018\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: required\n+asset_ids: ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON,ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS\n+asset_brief: Reserve original campaign asset groups for later approved implementation; authoring creates no asset.\n+visual_style_version: unselected-gate-0004\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define assembly of one versioned original campaign package that references the\n+town, dungeon, and character asset groups and connects the SHARD-02 domain\n+contracts to the existing content and provenance controls. Reserve assets only;\n+do not create product expression during authoring.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0005 owns schema, validation, registry, and package loading. R0011 owns the\n+provenance record and mandatory human creative-review disposition. R0013\u2013R0016\n+provide the content-neutral domain contracts referenced by the package. This\n+contract assembles their allowed references without changing their owners.\n+GATE-0004 and the human provenance review block implementation/admission of\n+concrete authored content; neither is resolved here.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `content/campaign/`, `assets/source-manifest.*`, and\n+  `tests/content/campaign*`.\n+- Campaign package assembly, stable content references, and provenance-manifest\n+  entries for the reserved asset groups.\n+- Content package loader integration using the R0005 validation boundary.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Assemble a versioned package for exactly one town, one dungeon, and the\n+campaign's character/content references. Every expressive package entry must\n+have a stable content ID, package reference, and complete provenance record as\n+defined by R0011. The loader admits only a package whose references resolve,\n+whose provenance is complete, and whose human creative-review disposition is\n+recorded as ready; it must reject missing, unmatched, or unreviewed entries.\n+The package must use the predecessor contracts' stable IDs rather than define\n+new gameplay rules. A reviewer may hold or reject the package; automated checks\n+cannot claim creative, legal, licensing, or GATE-0004 approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The same validated package is consumed by web and installed-PWA adapters.\n+Rendering, responsive presentation, packaging, caching, and download behavior\n+remain owned by later UI/PWA work and do not bypass provenance validation.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create, generate, source, select, or approve artwork, maps, characters,\n+dialogue, localisation, music, sound effects, licences, or copied expression.\n+Do not add regions, UI, PWA delivery, or legal approval; do not resolve\n+GATE-0004 or the human review.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `required`. Reserve only these stable product asset groups:\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN` (one original town environment),\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON` (one original dungeon environment), and\n+`ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS` (original campaign character expression). They\n+appear only through package references and provenance entries; their source of\n+truth is the later approved asset/content implementation. Required variants,\n+visual style, and original-art acceptance remain unselected under\n+`unselected-gate-0004`. Authoring creates no files or product assets. Before\n+admission, each eventual asset must have complete provenance and an explicit\n+human creative-review disposition; technical validation is not approval.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no campaign cue is selected or integrated\n+by this assembly contract. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and\n+style version blank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Validate a synthetic, non-product package whose town/dungeon/character\n+  references resolve through R0005 and whose domain references are stable.\n+- Prove absent provenance, unmatched references, invalid disposition, or a\n+  package not marked ready after human review is rejected before admission.\n+- Check that the three reserved IDs, asset brief, and style placeholder match\n+  IMP-0018 and the manifest, with no asset created; retain GATE-0004 and the\n+  recorded human provenance-review requirement.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain package-validator results, rejected provenance fixtures, the synthetic\n+human-review disposition, asset-reservation comparison, and both gate records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The versioned package resolves only validated, stable campaign references.\n+- Every expressive entry requires complete provenance and a recorded human\n+  creative-review disposition before admission.\n+- Only the three manifest-defined asset IDs are reserved; no product asset,\n+  copied expression, or creative/legal approval is created or claimed.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f5e8b01a9832de3d4e34d0d94d13fdd7966cd52b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0019.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0019\n+sequence: 19\n+title: Add campaign domain invariant and negative-fixture coverage\n+dependencies: R0013,R0014,R0015,R0016\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,NFR-0007\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#2-exploration-town-dungeon-and-campaign-content,specification/02-feature-model.md#4-party-combat-encounters-rewards-and-balance\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0019\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; deterministic invalid-state fixtures only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Add deterministic shared-core negative fixtures and cross-domain invariants for\n+the SHARD-02 campaign contracts. The work proves that invalid references,\n+blocked routes, stale commands, and duplicate grants are detected without\n+introducing concrete campaign content.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0013 supplies scene/exit validation, R0014 quest transitions, R0015 encounter\n+and reward resolution, and R0016 inventory/party protection. This contract owns\n+fixtures and invariant assertions only; it does not change their APIs or state\n+rules. GATE-0004 remains explicit for concrete content assumptions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/core/campaign/fixtures/` and `tests/core/campaign/invariants*`.\n+- Deterministic negative campaign fixtures and fixture builders.\n+- Cross-contract invariant assertions and repeat-safety coverage.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Provide deterministic fixture builders for unresolved scene, quest, encounter,\n+reward, item, predicate, and route references; blocked and dead-end routes;\n+stale revisions; and duplicate interaction/reward IDs. Each fixture has a\n+stable expected rejection or invariant result. Assert that invalid inputs never\n+mutate campaign state, required completion routes remain reachable in valid\n+abstract fixtures, and retries do not duplicate rewards or progression. Keep\n+fixtures content-neutral and isolated from player data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+These are shared-core test fixtures. They do not test browser rendering, input,\n+responsive UI, service workers, cache behavior, or installed-PWA lifecycle.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create product maps, dialogue, characters, combatants, assets, audio,\n+real player data, browser-matrix tests, UI, persistence drivers, or concrete\n+content values. Do not resolve GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: deterministic invalid-state fixtures require\n+no product visual/source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\n+textures, portraits, fonts, or other incidental assets; `asset_ids` is blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: fixtures own no music or sound-effect\n+trigger. Keep audio metadata blank/default and do not create test or product\n+cues.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run every fixture twice and prove byte-for-byte equivalent result, including\n+  unchanged state for invalid reference, blocked route, and stale-command cases.\n+- Prove duplicate interaction/reward IDs never apply twice and a valid abstract\n+  fixture has a reachable completion path with no protected-item dead end.\n+- Compare requirements, dependencies, ownership, and provenance against\n+  IMP-0019 and the manifest; retain GATE-0004 for concrete assumptions.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fixture output, invariant failures/rejections, repeat-run\n+comparison, reachability output, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Every invalid campaign reference and blocked route has deterministic detected\n+  coverage and does not mutate state.\n+- Valid abstract progression has no dead end; stale commands and duplicate\n+  grants are repeat-safe.\n+- Fixtures introduce no player data, browser coverage, product assets, audio,\n+  or concrete content, while GATE-0004 remains explicit.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a972ced7298533227a772ac88cd7240691489440\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0020.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0020\n+sequence: 20\n+title: Document SHARD-02 ownership, gates, and handoff boundaries\n+dependencies: R0017,R0018,R0019\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0012\n+source_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership,specification/02-feature-model.md#capability-parity-and-intentional-differences\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0020\n+authoring_batch: B0008\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; documentation and SHARD-03 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Document the SHARD-02 campaign-domain ownership index, unresolved gates,\n+asset/provenance handoff, and explicit boundary to SHARD-03. This is a\n+developer-documentation contract and does not implement UI or PWA behaviour.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0017 documents the progression integration, R0018 documents package assembly\n+and asset/provenance reservation, and R0019 documents invariant coverage. This\n+handoff records their interfaces and limits without assuming their completion\n+resolves GATE-0004 or human review.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/campaign-domain-boundary.md`.\n+- SHARD-02 ownership index, retained-gate register, and SHARD-03 handoff.\n+- Documented handoff for campaign-domain contracts and validated package input.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Record the owner and public boundary for scenes/exits, quest/tutorial state,\n+encounters/rewards, inventory/party progression, campaign completion, content\n+package/provenance, and campaign negative fixtures. State that GATE-0004 blocks\n+concrete authored campaign implementation and that human creative/provenance\n+review is mandatory before content admission; neither is an automated or\n+documentation approval. Identify SHARD-03 as the owner of session, UI, input,\n+accessibility, responsive presentation, and browser/PWA adaptation, while the\n+shared core supplies deterministic commands/state only.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Document the intentional boundary: responsive web and installed PWA consume\n+the same campaign rules and validated content, but their UI, input adapters,\n+cache/install/update lifecycle, and release delivery are not SHARD-02 work.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement UI, PWA delivery, browser tests, rendering, input mappings,\n+asset production, audio, release claims, product changes, or gate approvals.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this documentation creates no visual or\n+source asset. Do not create or reserve any product asset; `asset_ids` remains\n+blank. R0018 remains the sole owner of its reserved campaign asset IDs.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: no cue, playback behavior, or mix belongs\n+to this documentation handoff. Keep audio metadata blank/default and create no\n+audio asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Cross-check the ownership index against IMP-0013 through IMP-0020 and\n+  R0013\u2013R0019, confirming every shared domain has one stated owner/boundary.\n+- Confirm GATE-0004, human provenance review, R0018 asset reservation, and the\n+  SHARD-03 UI/PWA boundary are explicit and unresolved where required.\n+- Compare metadata, requirement IDs, dependencies, provenance, and ownership\n+  with IMP-0020 and the manifest without making release-readiness claims.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the ownership cross-check, gate/provenance review record, SHARD-03\n+handoff review, and manifest/catalogue comparison.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The documentation assigns SHARD-02 domain ownership and its interfaces\n+  without claiming UI or PWA implementation ownership.\n+- GATE-0004, the human provenance review, and R0018 asset-reservation boundary\n+  are explicit and unresolved.\n+- SHARD-03 receives a clear documented handoff for UI, input, accessibility,\n+  responsive web, and installed-PWA responsibilities.\n\ntokens used\n65,370\n", "adapter_log": "", "test_log": "Validator: 0 missing R files, 0 unverified contracts; 3 reserved R0018 asset IDs.", "browser_log": "No browser/UI/PWA scope is owned by these contracts.", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Exactly R0017 through R0020 are created, each mapping only to its assigned `IMP-*` record.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Created R0017\u2192IMP-0017, R0018\u2192IMP-0018, R0019\u2192IMP-0019, and R0020\u2192IMP-0020 only; validator reports no missing or unallocated contracts."}, {"criterion": "Every generated R file h